{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'cat task/task_contract.json; cat results/ideas/03_checkpoint_weighted_flip_path_exchange/program_1/src/IMPLEMENTATION.md'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"canonical_task\": {\n    \"path\": \"task.md\",\n    \"sha256\": \"e4935f14c47be3f40dba4b1e04f0cc983f4d8d35b139befe19b98f5b4ec88e67\"\n  },\n  \"method\": {\n    \"class\": \"Influence-guided outcome-flip sensitivity analysis of regularized Bradley-Terry rankings, verified by independent exact refits\",\n    \"description\": \"{\\\"aggregation\\\": \\\"Within episode equal mean of three nonzero edit budgets (1/3 each); equal seeds within case (1/3 production, identity smoke); Arena single crowd case identity; NBA equal seasons (1/3 search,1/5 final); equal family weights1/2,1/2. Each Arena seed weight1/6, each NBA search seed-case1/18, final1/30 before budget. Random baselines average streams first (4 search,8 final,1 smoke). All failed/missing episodes retain zero score/baseline/displacement and influence_error=control_error=1, validity/correct=0 at original weights. Method-audit failure retains zero candidate score/displacement and influence_error1. Flags are conjunctions, not means. No survivor renormalization.\\\", \\\"audits\\\": \\\"Independent trusted Newton fitting max100 iterations, max35 line-search backtracks, gradient infinity norm <2e-7; ridge1; candidate scores/audit derivatives/directional influences/prefix shift arithmetic allclose atol2e-5 rtol2e-4 (scores) or3e-3 (derivatives). Eight deterministic evenly spaced audit rows; finite difference epsilon1e-3, derivative allclose atol2e-5 rtol3e-3. This verifies executable influence arithmetic and independent fit/selection outputs, not hidden candidate internals. Nonlinear exact-refit prediction discrepancy norm/(1+norm) is reported as influence_error, not a superiority or linear-accuracy threshold.\\\", \\\"baselines\\\": \\\"Uniform random eligible flips; degree-sum quartile-stratified random flips matching each prefix of ACTUAL candidate selected row degree bins (approximate exposure matching, not exact endpoint matching); smallest absolute fitted matchup margin heuristic. Equal edit budgets, observed inputs and fixed random streams; baselines receive no candidate-only feedback. Streams seeded episode_seed+8371; actual degree matching seed+72831; grouped bootstrap seed+49207. Candidate may select alternative nested feasible sets; numerical directional influence/audit calculations and predicted prefix shifts must remain genuine.\\\", \\\"controls\\\": \\\"Canonical controls declared before scoring: (1) evaluator copy/no-op refit identical scores atol1e-9; (2) evaluator constant-zero predictor must be rejected by known nonzero exact-refit shift >.01 on explicitly synthetic 3-game 2-participant diagnostic, never substituted for real-data evidence; (3) rotate eligible directional priorities by one, require nonidentity priorities, different selected row set AND nonidentical refitted coefficients atol1e-9; matched budgets, no superiority gate; vacuity retains failed/inconclusive control; (4) immediately after required reset, analyze token input without data returns exactly error:no_data so previously legal state cannot be reused. Four control types weight1/4 each, each has one conjunction assertion. No controls expose labels, metrics or reference results via candidate RPC.\\\", \\\"deadlines\\\": \\\"One invocation deadline starts before loading, subtract conservative startup allowance120s search/300s final, reserve finish60s/120s. All episode resets globally reserve2s plus8s worst-case overhead each, including sequential candidate+worker termination/reap/stderr teardown. Each production episode reserves reference four methods30s each, candidate30s, scoring/controls/uncertainty90s search (=240 productive allowance); final90s each reference/candidate and210s scoring (=660). Ref methods have individual work alarms; parent reference worker total122/362 bounds, with explicit3s dispatch slack. Same candidate30/90 allowance per method, fixed estimator and edits. Each remaining reset reservation is retained on timeout. No canonical minimum productive baseline time exists. Actual productive reference work is measured excluding startup/imports/reset/output. Reduced smoke120s total subtracts2s startup,3s finish, reset2s+overhead2s each, reference individual1s/total5s, candidate1s, scoring4s with1 replicate; same cases/order/operations/loading/imports/isolation. Smoke does not attest production feasibility.\\\", \\\"final_correct\\\": \\\"Separately require all final cases/seeds/transcript and the same operational/scientific validity checks on sealed data. No comparative-superiority requirement. Final claim assessment uses paired effects/uncertainty and manuscript review; unsubstantiated superiority claims must be removed, not retroactively made search vetoes. Paper novelty/acceptance is NOT automated by numeric correct.\\\", \\\"limitations\\\": \\\"Operational proxy does not itself write/review the required conference PDF/LaTeX/checklist, assess novelty, inspect forbidden literature, prove opaque hidden mechanisms or establish causality across unequal comparison graphs. Publication requires human/scientific evidence review of actual manuscript and reproducibility artifacts. No held-out predictive-target task, adaptation requirement or learning/state-hash gate is invented. Methods optimize feasible observed-outcome perturbations, not historical misconduct. Fixed regularization, fractional ties, graph coverage, coarse degree matching and fixed intervention plans in bootstrap bound interpretation. Final data/outcomes cannot be used for search tuning.\\\", \\\"operational\\\": \\\"Linux x86-64 CPython3.11-3.13 (draft tested3.12), libseccomp.so.2, Landlock ABI>=3 for native validation; no GPU. 4 CPU cores/8GiB aggregate, at most2 active compute cores/threads and4GiB per role. Explicit thread environment, native/trusted subprocess address-space limits and all-thread CPU ceiling ceil(2*plane_wall), killable monotonic wall transport. Harness owns isolated production quotas. Native candidate has clean allowlisted environment, private copied single-file source and Landlock filesystem/seccomp network isolation; no evaluator resources/results/credentials mount. Only fixed proxy path plus socket authenticates in-process broker loading; proxy calls use bounded alarm, never child-launched. Final standalone requires own file, own resources and installed dependencies/harness only.\\\", \\\"operations_per_episode\\\": {\\\"analyze\\\": 1, \\\"download_chunk_max\\\": 16, \\\"reset\\\": 1, \\\"reset_probe_analyze_no_data\\\": 1, \\\"upload_chunk_max\\\": 16, \\\"upload_commit\\\": 1, \\\"upload_start\\\": 1}, \\\"rpc_derivation\\\": \\\"37 per episode using declared maximum 16 input and 16 output chunks, including setup/commit even for one chunk. Search 4 cases x3 seeds x37=444. Final 6 cases x3 seeds x37=666. No replay, retries, export/import state transfer, extra training or diagnostic resets. Evaluator-only copy/constant/permutation/refit/bootstrap operations use zero broker calls; reset control is the counted probe. Mock maximum transcript and scheduler/failure tests precede production.\\\", \\\"scientific_workload\\\": \\\"Arena: all 14272 search and 43205 final usable comparisons; NBA all unique games in 2006-2008 search and 2011-2015 final, season-specific participant universes. No Elo inputs. Sum logistic loss plus 0.5*L2 norm squared, ridge=1 for participant and optional home coefficients, centered participant scores; ties y=.5 included in fitting but cannot be edited. Fractions .001,.005,.01 of ALL usable rows, floor to integer, binary outcome flips, distinct nested prefix sets. A zero positive-budget edit count is invalid. Deterministic tie order is participant index in lexicographically sorted source names.\\\", \\\"search_correct\\\": \\\"Complete planned search reset transcript; valid bounded protocol and content-provenance integrity; feasible actual nested row edits; genuine numerically audited influence arithmetic; successful converged independent fits, required baselines and all nonvacuous controls; complete finite fixed-weight evidence; no isolation/leakage/resource violation. No large-sensitivity or baseline-superiority threshold. scientific_valid records mandatory estimator/method/control completeness; correct additionally requires operational/integrity completion. Eligible candidates ranked descending combined_score. A schema-valid state_changed or other self-report never contributes evidence.\\\", \\\"uncertainty\\\": \\\"Arena raw-document connected components and NBA unique games are grouped bootstrap units within each fixed panel, 10 search and30 final replicates per case/seed (1 smoke). Bootstrap original and fixed candidate/baseline nested interventions paired under identical group multiplicity weights; all random streams participate. Report 2.5/97.5 percentile rank intervals and paired candidate-minus-baseline effects. Failed required refits/resamples preserve entire episode worst-case evidence rather than intervals over survivors. Three seeds are algorithmic variation, not independent datasets. Sports conclusions are descriptive of fixed seasons, not causal effects of design.\\\", \\\"wire\\\": \\\"Only finite inline JSON lines, no paths or shared files. little-endian float64 observed [n,4] a,b,y,z, maximum input/output decoded size 16MiB each in candidate RAM, chunk 1MiB max, maximum 16 chunks each direction; participant cap256, n cap524288. Every actual line plus representative request_id/payload/error envelope and LF framing is serialized and checked <8MiB locally and strictly <64MiB harness limit. Full-sized representative base64 chunks preflight at 1398185 bytes or less including line metadata; larger framing has more than 56MiB unused harness headroom.\\\"}\"\n  },\n  \"candidate\": {\n    \"interface\": \"python_rpc_v1:handle\",\n    \"editable_paths\": [\n      \"program_0/src\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"evaluators\": {\n    \"search\": \"evaluate.py\",\n    \"final\": \"evaluate_final.py\"\n  },\n  \"resources\": {\n    \"search_root\": \"resources/search\",\n    \"final_root\": \"resources/final\",\n    \"public_artifact_bundle\": null\n  },\n  \"data\": {\n    \"search_roles\": [\n      \"search_observed_comparisons\",\n      \"search_normalized_provenance\"\n    ],\n    \"final_roles\": [\n      \"final_observed_comparisons\",\n      \"final_normalized_provenance\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"metrics\": {\n    \"search\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"combined_score\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"random_flip_score\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"degree_matched_score\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"margin_heuristic_score\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"mean_rank_displacement\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"influence_error\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"control_error\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"scientific_valid\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"correct\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_observed_comparisons\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"final\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"combined_score\",\n        \"data_role\": \"final_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"random_flip_score\",\n        \"data_role\": \"final_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"degree_matched_score\",\n        \"data_role\": \"final_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"margin_heuristic_score\",\n        \"data_role\": \"final_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"mean_rank_displacement\",\n        \"data_role\": \"final_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"influence_error\",\n        \"data_role\": \"final_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"control_error\",\n        \"data_role\": \"final_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"scientific_valid\",\n        \"data_role\": \"final_observed_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"correct\",\n        \"data_role\": \"final_observed_comparisons\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"upstream\": [\n    {\n      \"repository\": \"https://huggingface.co/datasets/lmarena-ai/arena-human-preference-55k\",\n      \"revision\": \"18c298340948c0e7f7727399fd459cca6ce0ca6f\",\n      \"package_version\": null,\n      \"license\": \"Apache-2.0\",\n      \"entrypoints\": [\n        \"train.csv\"\n      ],\n      \"patches\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"repository\": \"https://github.com/fivethirtyeight/data\",\n      \"revision\": \"4c1ff5e3aef1816ae04af63218015066e186c147\",\n      \"package_version\": null,\n      \"license\": \"CC-BY-4.0\",\n      \"entrypoints\": [\n        \"nba-elo/nbaallelo.csv\"\n      ],\n      \"patches\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"provenance\": {\n    \"dependencies\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"numpy\",\n        \"version\": \"2.2.6\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"scipy\",\n        \"version\": \"1.15.3\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"matplotlib\",\n        \"version\": \"3.10.3\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"artifacts\": [\n      {\n        \"role\": \"sealed_final_benchmark\",\n        \"path\": \"resources/final/arena.json\",\n        \"sha256\": \"5f09a6fab5e9bc34b31d49d3413d8399f205d368fcd3f566b3be5fbef8976959\",\n        \"source\": \"Derived by pre