48256ab900a45123e2d568c06007873227d2\",\n        \"source\": \"Derived by prepare_data.py from checksum-verified fixed Arena/NBA snapshots. Contains observed comparisons and normalized document/example hashes, not raw conversation text.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"search_benchmark\",\n        \"path\": \"resources/search/nba-2008.json\",\n        \"sha256\": \"da24ea302d9eedc090da7c2247ded80b0dcbe83ff72705b75cae94b6e2451f15\",\n        \"source\": \"Derived by prepare_data.py from checksum-verified fixed Arena/NBA snapshots. Contains observed comparisons and normalized document/example hashes, not raw conversation text.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"reproducible_preparation\",\n        \"path\": \"prepare_data.py\",\n        \"sha256\": \"e2958fe33c11c41519f2e2c336c3767df87cb0c2c0313b8dd26c705cd5671838\",\n        \"source\": \"Task-authored deterministic raw-source checksum, normalized document/example union-find split and reciprocal-game audit.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"pinned_direct_dependencies\",\n        \"path\": \"requirements.txt\",\n        \"sha256\": \"393d9162235ee3676b301ed71a254a322c488be9c7ac3c4928ec5e23cee085f1\",\n        \"source\": \"Exact identities/versions verified against https://pypi.org/pypi/numpy/2.2.6/json, https://pypi.org/pypi/scipy/1.15.3/json and https://pypi.org/pypi/matplotlib/3.10.3/json.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"harness_compatibility\",\n        \"path\": \"capture.py\",\n        \"sha256\": \"9ccd8975f287cca981934eb4fdb5ff223a1c26d15056396da67338fd77d556c6\",\n        \"source\": \"Task-authored safe OutputCapture compatibility artifact.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"search_evaluator\",\n        \"path\": \"evaluate.py\",\n        \"sha256\": \"321cf0812a35e81d232de440a1845b5e93c2a4eacb9d2c690d083d1f1937a062\",\n        \"source\": \"Task-authored self-contained independent regularized Newton refits and bounded evaluator-owned controls.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"role\": \"sealed_final_evaluator\",\n        \"path\": \"evaluate_final.py\",\n        \"sha256\": \"39ba2cda512794e4cb13737549cc52e87aa77b771315eb73facd215d973f2833\",\n        \"source\": \"Task-authored self-contained sealed evaluator. No search imports or search resource reads.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"compute\": {\n    \"search\": {\n      \"accelerator\": \"cpu\",\n      \"accelerator_model\": \"none\",\n      \"gpu_count\": 0,\n      \"evaluator_gpu_count\": 0,\n      \"candidate_gpu_count\": 0,\n      \"cpu_cores\": 4,\n      \"memory_gb\": 8,\n      \"precision\": \"float64\",\n      \"wall_clock_seconds\": 3600,\n      \"max_candidate_rpc_calls\": 444\n    },\n    \"final\": {\n      \"accelerator\": \"cpu\",\n      \"accelerator_model\": \"none\",\n      \"gpu_count\": 0,\n      \"evaluator_gpu_count\": 0,\n      \"candidate_gpu_count\": 0,\n      \"cpu_cores\": 4,\n      \"memory_gb\": 8,\n      \"precision\": \"float64\",\n      \"wall_clock_seconds\": 14400,\n      \"max_candidate_rpc_calls\": 666\n    }\n  },\n  \"protocol\": {\n    \"search_seeds\": [\n      101,\n      211,\n      307\n    ],\n    \"final_seeds\": [\n      401,\n      503,\n      607\n    ],\n    \"search_reset_sequence\": [\n      101,\n      101,\n      101,\n      101,\n      211,\n      211,\n      211,\n      211,\n      307,\n      307,\n      307,\n      307\n    ],\n    \"search_smoke_reset_sequence\": [\n      101,\n      101,\n      101,\n      101\n    ],\n    \"final_reset_sequence\": [\n      401,\n      401,\n      401,\n      401,\n      401,\n      401,\n      503,\n      503,\n      503,\n      503,\n      503,\n      503,\n      607,\n      607,\n      607,\n      607,\n      607,\n      607\n    ],\n    \"final_smoke_reset_sequence\": [\n      401,\n      401,\n      401,\n      401,\n      401,\n      401\n    ],\n    \"baselines\": [\n      \"unmodified_copy\",\n      \"uniform_random_flips\",\n      \"degree_sum_quartile_matched_flips\",\n      \"close_margin_heuristic\",\n      \"synthetic_constant_zero\",\n      \"permuted_influence_priorities\",\n      \"reset_no_data\"\n    ],\n    \"promotion_rule\": \"Development-only integrity-eligible ranking by descending combined_score, ties earlier submission then digest. At most three complete search submissions, one frozen sealed final invocation; harness exclusively owns promotion/freezing/publication. No comparative threshold, final-feedback tuning, replay or retries.\",\n    \"search_proxies\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"smaller_content_panel\",\n        \"preserves\": \"Real crowdsourced preferences, normalized document groups, genuine binary flips and independent fixed-L2 BT refits, all four controls and both evaluation designs.\",\n        \"omits\": \"Remaining sealed Arena groups and later NBA seasons; cannot establish temporal generalization or publication-quality evidence alone.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"lighter_uncertainty\",\n        \"preserves\": \"Fixed paired group bootstrap, fixed weights, matched edit budgets and all planned cases/seeds.\",\n        \"omits\": \"Final uses 8 instead of4 random streams,30 instead of10 resamples and five instead of three sports seasons.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"feedback\": {\n    \"search_visible\": [\n      \"Search scalar metrics and correctness, validated search-only solution evidence; fixed bounded failure categories. Raw worker stderr is repair-only under exact drafting/qualification flags.\",\n      \"Observed search episode comparison endpoints/outcomes and public workload/model settings through documented RPC only.\"\n    ],\n    \"final_sealed\": [\n      \"Final resource panels, manifests, seed constants, reference fits, metrics, correctness, controls and solution evidence are sealed until freeze and never optimization feedback.\",\n      \"During final execution candidate receives only observed final comparisons and plane-independent workload/model inputs, never held-out answers, scores or baseline outputs.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"publication\": {\n    \"search_is_proxy\": true,\n    \"requires_final_evaluation\": true,\n    \"required_evidence\": [\n      \"A complete research paper, PDF and LaTeX source in the latest officially released NeurIPS main-conference template available when preparing the submission; document the chosen edition and comply with its actual page limit and required checklist. Include abstract, introduction, genuinely read related work, intervention/model methods, real-data experiments, uncertainty, discussion, limitations and references. Obtain and record official template provenance downstream; no template or completed paper is claimed to exist at design time.\",\n      \"Real results on both the crowdsourced Arena panel and season-specific NBA panels, including every declared case/seed/budget, baseline stream and control, with normalized edit-cost definitions, why two different designs are comparable, graph/participant coverage and clear limits from unequal data volumes, temporal change, ties, home advantage, regularization and non-causal cross-design comparisons. Report null and adverse results equally. Do not imply that these datasets represent all leaderboards or identify malicious behavior.\",\n      \"Verified pinned-source checksums and licenses, raw-data acquisition instructions, evaluator-owned source IDs and row provenance, normalization specification, complete raw-document/example SHA-256 manifests and demonstrated search/final content disjointness before feature extraction. Document reciprocal NBA rows, excluded invalid records, connectedness and split-induced selection. Raw data stays in working data storage, not the code repository or paper submission; do not redistribute private split material or unnecessary text. Source checksums quoted in task.md are expected values, not design-time verification evidence.\",\n      \"Reproducible genuine candidate influence computation and trusted independent Bradley-Terry reference/refit code; fixed estimator and edit-feasibility policy; finite-difference and actual-refit audits; matched-budget baseline/control results including rejected vacuous permutations and reset-state tests. Pairwise comparative claims require the corresponding baseline contrasts and uncertainty. Missing or failed evidence retains finite worst-case values, full fixed weights and explicit failure status. No comparison advantage, stability conclusion or causal alignment result may be inferred from an incomplete or vacuous control.\",\n      \"Separate reports of scientific validity, search eligibility and final claim assessment, including exact search and final correct predicates, score hierarchy and weights, predeclared tie policy, all three-or-fewer search submissions and failures, frozen candidate digest/configuration, final unsealing chronology and the single final invocation. Novelty and publication standards are not post hoc search thresholds. State which narrower claims remain justified if comparisons are inconclusive.\",\n      \"Downstream contract preflight with canonical task digest, actual source/dependency provenance and synchronized artifact hashes; exact production/smoke reset arrays matching case/seed cardinality and order globally across clients/restarts; no unplanned resets or replays; actual largest production request/response JSON serialization sizes including UTF-8, base64, metadata, envelope and framing; bounded candidate-RAM chunk sessions; and fully counted max_candidate_rpc_calls covering resets, stale-token checks, chunks, failures and retries. No shared filesystem or path-based RPC. This design specifies required evidence; it does not claim preflight has already passed.\",\n      \"Offline smoke validation for both planes through unchanged loader/import/device/mount/broker/update/metric paths with reduced work, empty HOME and the exact smoke transcripts. Keep smoke validation distinct from successful full production completion. Provide harness allocation/isolation evidence, all-thread CPU policy, actual monotonic times and cleanup/cancellation logs. Clearly distinguish enforced wall/RPC/resource ceilings from advisory candidate-internal iteration counts; do not present reported iteration counters as a trusted hard operation cap.\",\n      \"All paper numbers, plots and tables must come from actual recorded task runs with scripts mapping each output to inputs, seeds, configuration and trusted metrics. Provide code, standard requirements.txt versions, offline wheel/platform instructions, data-fetch commands, reproduction commands and measured or honestly labeled estimated runtimes. Log failures, abandoned approaches, unfinished analyses and LLM assistance. Never fabricate checkpoints, measurements, successful launches, read literature or completed validation.\",\n      \"Respect the canonical independence restriction: never identify, guess, search for, access or use the prohibited prior paper or any related mirror, abstract, discussion, reproduction or code. Use only explicitly allowed starter readings and unrelated permitted sources, avoid broad searches likely to encounter forbidden material, and immediately stop and record any accidental encounter with location and amount read. Network is restricted to listed data acquisition, permissible literature and dependency installation; no paid APIs. Finish research, experiments, writing and reproduction within the one-week task budget.\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n# Interface-compatible scope\n\nThe starter's only input is an inline float64 table of participant indices,\noutcomes, and a home covariate. Its only intervention is a nested sequence of\ndistinct binary outcome flips. This implementation does not reinterpret flips as\ndeletions and does not infer dataset identities, prompts, annotators, response\nidentities, or clusters from anonymous rows.\n\nConsequently the proposed matched human/GPT-4 study, whole-question deletion,\nreal-data acquisition, cluster bootstrap, supported-ordering intervals, random\ndeletion controls, and paper production are not implemented. The stage forbids\nthe acquisition and experimental runs needed to support those claims. No\nempirical results, confidence guarantees, or causal judge-type claims are made.\n\n## Implemented adaptation\n\n- The sum-loss, fixed-ridge Bradley-Terry objective and optional home nuisance\n  are unchanged. Half-win ties remain in every fit and are never selected.\n- Sufficient statistics aggregate equal design rows without deleting or\n  deduplicating genuine observations. Each selectable unit remains one original\n  binary observation. Grouping by design and original outcome permits exact\n  accounting of flip capacity while avoiding a dense observation-by-parameter\n  matrix.\n- Fits use damped Newton steps with Cholesky solves, an L-BFGS fallback, and a\n  stationarity check. Flips change win sufficient statistics, not observation\n  counts or ridge strength. Every candidate ordering used in search is refitted;\n  no first-order shift is treated as a finite-change ranking.\n- A deterministic width-two search adapts priorities at the three requested\n  checkpoints. Branches include the prescribed frozen contrast and up to six\n  currently close, baseline-oriented participant contrasts. Closeness is only a\n  search heuristic, not a confidence interval. Branches are compared by summed\n  exact rank displacement across checkpoints, then inversions, then a smooth\n  inversion potential. The original fixed-influence path is retained as a\n  candidate. This is bounded heuristic search, not an optimality certificate or\n  a claim of a successful reversal.\n- All public influences, eight audit derivatives, and three predicted shifts\n  still use the original fitted Hessian and the documented frozen contrast.\n  Predictions are linear approximations even though search uses exact refits.\n  Internal search scores never appear in the response.\n- Reset, upload, analyze, and download responses and the float64 result layout\n  are unchanged. The implementation is self-contained in `program.py`; this\n  document is not required at runtime.\n\n## Checkpoint-local complete-path refinement\n\nThe width-two search above is retained unchanged as the incumbent generator.\nIts complete returned path is scored first using the same lexicographic sum of\ncheckpoint displacement, inversions, and smooth inversion potential. Duplicate\nbudgets retain their original multiplicity in that sum. This internal objective\nis not assumed to equal the harness's combined score.\n\nThe optional search considers both selected-position swaps and replacements by\nunused original binary rows. For a swap at zero-based positions `left < right`,\nonly budgets `left < budget <= right` change; for a replacement at `position`,\nonly budgets `budget > position` change. Unaffected checkpoint scores are reused.\nThe fitter and its convergence check are unchanged; each new prefix set is fitted\nwith the original ridge and baseline warm start. Request-local caches use sorted\noriginal-row tuples, not dataset identities, ordering-dependent keys, or influence\npredictions. Equivalent design types only screen proposals and identify the\nlowest-index unused representative; they do not replace original-row cache keys.\n\nScreening uses current fitted rank gaps in the existing smooth potential and the\noriginal fitted inverse Hessian. Each sweep samples up to 24 evenly spaced path\npositions plus checkpoint boundaries. At a position it screens all selected\npartners and one unused representative of each binary design/outcome type,\nthen exactly scores the best screened swap and replacement when available.\nStrict complete-score improvement alone permits acceptance. The sweep restarts\nafter acceptance with a rotated position cursor so it visits other sampled\npositions before repeatedly revisiting the same position. This is heuristic\nscreening, not exhaustive exchange optimization or an optimality certificate.\n\nAfter the incumbent is fully scored, optional work is capped at 128 proposals,\n72 additional converged refits for dimensions at most 64 (24 otherwise), and a\ntwo-second soft deadline checked before proposals and uncached fits. An ongoing\nfit is not interrupted; the deadline is not a hard total-runtime guarantee.\nProposal screening and traversal are deterministic, but the deadline can truncate\nthe accepted search prefix differently under different machine loads.\nIncomplete/nonfinite proposals are never compared as complete scores. Numerical\nor optional-search failure returns the best fully accepted path, or the original\nincumbent if none was accepted. No cache, counters, scores, or errors extend the\npublic response. Actual returned paths are checked for uniqueness, original-row\nbounds, binary outcomes, and coverage of every requested checkpoint.\n\nThe live refinement path includes small synthetic prefix-set checks for every\nswap and replacement on a four-row path, including repeated checkpoint budgets.\nThese compare local updates against full checkpoint prefix-set recomputation;\nthey are structural checks, not scientific data or independent fitter validation.\n\n## Validation status\n\nOnly static source inspection was permitted during preparation. No candidate\ncode, tests, benchmarks, optimizers, or evaluation was executed. Runtime,\nnumerical agreement with an independent fitter, and scientific effectiveness\nremain unmeasured; the harness owns the subsequent evaluation. No external\nliterature or prohibited research source was accessed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
