{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"jq -r '.method.description | fromjson | .scientific_workload' task/task_contract.json; jq '{normalization,group_rule,content_disjoint,source_disjoint,cases:(.cases | map(del(.hashes,.rows)))}' task/resources/final/manifest.json\"","aggregated_output":"Arena: all 14272 search and 43205 final usable comparisons; NBA all unique games in 2006-2008 search and 2011-2015 final, season-specific participant universes. No Elo inputs. Sum logistic loss plus 0.5*L2 norm squared, ridge=1 for participant and optional home coefficients, centered participant scores; ties y=.5 included in fitting but cannot be edited. Fractions .001,.005,.01 of ALL usable rows, floor to integer, binary outcome flips, distinct nested prefix sets. A zero positive-budget edit count is invalid. Deterministic tie order is participant index in lexicographically sorted source names.\n{\n  \"normalization\": \"v1 NFC line endings preserve case/whitespace; additional NFKC whitespace-collapsed audit; JSON parsed before hashing; swapped example canonicalization; transitive document groups\",\n  \"group_rule\": \"sha256(split-v1:minimum-content-hash) modulo 4 equals 0 for search\",\n  \"content_disjoint\": true,\n  \"source_disjoint\": true,\n  \"cases\": [\n    {\n      \"groups\": 37842,\n      \"participants\": 64\n    },\n    {\n      \"groups\": 1311,\n      \"participants\": 30\n    },\n    {\n      \"groups\": 1074,\n      \"participants\": 30\n    },\n    {\n      \"groups\": 1314,\n      \"participants\": 30\n    },\n    {\n      \"groups\": 1319,\n      \"participants\": 30\n    },\n    {\n      \"groups\": 1311,\n      \"participants\": 30\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '1,58p' results/ideas/03_checkpoint_weighted_flip_path_exchange/program_1/src/program.py; jq '{keys:keys,reference_count:(.references | length)}' references_provenance.json; jq -r '.references[] | [.citation_key,.title,(has(\\\"read\\\")|tostring),(has(\\\"verification\\\")|tostring)] | @tsv' references_provenance.json | head -25; jq '.grounding_sources | to_entries[] | select(.key | startswith(\\\"final.qualification\\\"))' paper_data.json; ls figures; ls -d previous_paper aggregated extra_tasks 2>/dev/null; tail -20 memory.md; cat global_memory_summary.md | tail -25\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '1,58p' results/ideas/03_checkpoint_weighted_flip_path_exchange/program_1/src/program.py; jq '{keys:keys,reference_count:(.references | length)}' references_provenance.json; jq -r '.references[] | [.citation_key,.title,(has(\\\"read\\\")|tostring),(has(\\\"verification\\\")|tostring)] | @tsv' references_provenance.json | head -25; jq '.grounding_sources | to_entries[] | select(.key | startswith(\\\"final.qualification\\\"))' paper_data.json; ls figures; ls -d previous_paper aggregated extra_tasks 2>/dev/null; tail -20 memory.md; cat global_memory_summary.md | tail -25\"","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Exact-refit binary flips with bounded checkpoint-local path refinement.\n\nThe entrypoint is self-contained Python (installed NumPy/SciPy are available); native\nvalidation copies only this entrypoint into its private sandbox, not adjacent files.\nOnly handle(request)->finite JSON response is public. Extra response keys are forbidden.\nA reset accepts ANY nonnegative integer seed (not bool) and returns exactly {\"ok\":true};\nit clears all buffers, results and prior tokens. It does not choose dataset or workload.\nImmediately after reset, analyze({\"op\":\"analyze\",\"token\":\"input\"}) must return\nexactly {\"error\":\"no_data\"}; no data or prior proposal may survive reset.\n\nUpload protocol (all data inline; never paths):\n upload_start: token=\"input\", dtype=\"<f8\", shape=[n,4], byte_length=32*n,\n chunks=ceil(byte_length/1048576), participants=p, home=boolean. Response {\"ok\":true}.\n n<=524288, p in [2,256], chunks<=16; at most 16MiB decoded in-memory input.\n upload_chunk: token=\"input\", index=0..chunks-1, encoding=\"base64\", data=ASCII base64.\n Each chunk <=1048576 decoded bytes, in order. Response {\"ok\":true}.\n upload_commit: token=\"input\". Response {\"ok\":true}. Columns are participant indices\n a,b (integers represented as float64), observed y in {0,.5,1}, home covariate z in\n {-1,0,1}. No home nuisance is fitted if home=false. Ties fit as fractional outcomes\n but cannot be flipped. Inputs are observed comparisons, not held-out targets.\n analyze: token=\"input\", counts=[k1,k2,k3] positive nondecreasing exact edit budgets,\n audit_rows=list of 8 legal row indices, ridge=1.0, iterations=positive integer.\n The estimator minimizes SUM(logaddexp(0,x*theta)-y*x*theta)+ridge/2*||theta||^2,\n where x=e_a-e_b plus optional home coordinate z. Participant scores are centered.\n Returns {\"token\":\"result\",\"dtype\":\"<f8\",\"shape\":[L],\"byte_length\":8*L,\"chunks\":c}.\n download_chunk: token=\"result\", index=0..c-1. Returns exactly\n {\"index\":index,\"encoding\":\"base64\",\"data\":ASCII base64}, <=1MiB decoded/chunk.\n\nResult layout, concatenated little-endian float64 (d=p+int(home)):\n fitted theta[d]; directional row influences[n]; audit derivatives[8,d] row-major;\n ordered distinct selected binary row indices[max(counts)] as exact integer-valued\n floats; predicted shifts[3,d] row-major for the nested prefixes of those indices.\n L=d+n+8*d+max(counts)+3*d. No other diagnostics or fields are accepted.\n Target contrast t=e_lower-e_upper: sort participant scores decreasing with index as\n tie-break, among adjacent pairs in top min(10,p) choose smallest score gap (first\n gap breaks ties). Influence for row r is (1-2*y_r)*x_r @ inverse(H) @ t;\n audit derivative is inverse(H) @ x_r (UNIT outcome change, including ties).\n H is exact regularized Hessian at fitted theta. Predictions sum signed row\n derivatives for each selected prefix. Selection may improve on the starter's greedy\n priorities; actual refits, not claimed sensitivities, determine score. Exact influence\n arithmetic is audited independently; nonlinear approximation error is reported, not\n an advantage threshold. No claim of superiority is necessary for search eligibility.\n No objective, reference fit, baseline output or control feedback is returned.\n\nOperation order: reset, stale analyze, upload_start, chunks, upload_commit, analyze,\n download chunks. No export/import of persistent state, replay, filesystem sharing,\n or additional resets. All messages <64MiB including JSON/framing (local 8MiB cap).\n The runner owns resource limits. Internal iteration counts are advisory only.\n\"\"\"\nimport base64\nimport math\nimport time\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.linalg import cho_factor, cho_solve\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nfrom scipy.special import expit\n\n_state = {}\n{\n  \"keys\": [\n    \"campaign_results_dir\",\n    \"count\",\n    \"generated_at\",\n    \"queries\",\n    \"reference_query_plan\",\n    \"references\",\n    \"results_dir\"\n  ],\n  \"reference_count\": 25\n}\nKoh2017UnderstandingBP\tUnderstanding Black-box Predictions via Influence Functions\tfalse\tfalse\nSaunshi2022UnderstandingIF\tUnderstanding Influence Functions and Datamodels via Harmonic Analysis\tfalse\tfalse\nHusain2017ImprovingLI\tImproving Large-Scale Image Retrieval Through Robust Aggregation of Local Descriptors\tfalse\tfalse\nGao2016DemocraticDA\tDemocratic Diffusion Aggregation for Image Retrieval\tfalse\tfalse\nSmith1995ForagingSO\tForaging sociability of nesting wading birds (Ciconiiformes) at Lake Okeechobee, Florida\tfalse\tfalse\nNone\tPractical Image and Video Processing Using MATLAB\tfalse\tfalse\nLan2023QuantizationBA\tQuantization Bits Allocation for Wireless Federated Learning\tfalse\tfalse\nBratcher2018UsersOA\tUsers of a National Directory of PrEP Service Providers: Beliefs, Self-Efficacy, and Progress toward Prescription\tfalse\tfalse\nRidzuan2021ReviewOA\tReview on Aesthetic & Cosmetic Industries in Malaysia -A Way Forward\tfalse\tfalse\nZheng2025AHS\tA Hybrid Search Behavior-Based Adaptive Grey Wolf Optimizer for Cooperative Path Planning for Multiple UAVs\tfalse\tfalse\nXue2018EfficacyCO\tEfficacy characteristics of different therapeutic modalities for locally advanced prostate canc