{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"apply_patch() { python -c 'import pathlib,sys\nlines=sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\nassert lines[0]==\\\"*** Begin Patch\\\" and lines[-1]==\\\"*** End Patch\\\"\nposition=1\nwhile position<len(lines)-1:\n    assert lines[position].startswith(\\\"*** Add File: \\\"), \\\"Only new-file patches are supported\\\"\n    target=pathlib.Path(lines[position].split(\\\": \\\",1)[1]); position+=1; content=[]\n    while position<len(lines)-1 and not lines[position].startswith(\\\"*** Add File: \\\"):\n        assert lines[position].startswith(\\\"+\\\"); content.append(lines[position][1:]); position+=1\n    with target.open(\\\"x\\\",encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as output: output.write(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(content)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\n    print(\\\"Added\\\",target)\n'; }\napply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: paper_strategy.json\n+{\n+  \\\"status\\\": \\\"ready\\\",\n+  \\\"selected_prompt_family\\\": \\\"paper_standalone\\\",\n+  \\\"recommended_title\\\": \\\"Exact-Refit Stress Tests for Bradley–Terry Rankings\\\",\n+  \\\"central_question\\\": \\\"How much can small, matched-budget binary-outcome changes disrupt fitted Bradley–Terry orderings on the observed Arena and NBA panels, and how consistently do exact-refitted guided interventions exceed simple controls?\\\",\n+  \\\"central_thesis\\\": \\\"On the fixed Arena and NBA panels, influence-guided flip-path exchange yields larger budget-averaged pairwise-order disruption point estimates than three matched-budget baselines, but fixed-plan bootstrap evidence supports a clearer advantage on Arena than across NBA seasons.\\\",\n+  \\\"narrative_rationale\\\": \\\"The strongest evidence is the completed final evaluation of one selected outcome-flip method on two real evaluation designs, with independently refitted endpoints, three baselines, graph summaries and paired uncertainty. The paper should study attainable finite-perturbation sensitivity, not tell an improvement story or claim a certified robustness radius. The positive Arena contrasts and inconclusive sports contrasts jointly support a useful, bounded empirical-methodology study. The aggregate difference is not proof of a particular component's contribution or of a causal evaluation-design effect. Readiness here means a coherent framing is supported, not that publication, novelty or manuscript validation has been established.\\\",\n+  \\\"prior_paper_story_status\\\": \\\"rejected\\\",\n+  \\\"edit_framing_decision\\\": \\\"This is not edit mode: no resolved edit-context files, previous_paper manuscript, aggregated directory or extra_tasks directory is present. There is no prior manuscript story to preserve. The rejected alternative is the prospective exposure-matched MT-Bench block-deletion story recorded in planning, not an existing paper. Reject it as the main story because the implemented and evaluated intervention is anonymous binary-outcome flipping on Arena and NBA. Compare alternatives explicitly: local preservation of the prospective story lacks evaluated deletions and matching; broadening to a shared deletion/flip method would exceed the evidence; recentering on the evaluated finite-flip sensitivity question is supported. No previous title or figure plan is inherited.\\\",\n+  \\\"staged_input_impact\\\": [\n+    \\\"paper_data.json.final_evaluation was read independently: final.qualification.status is completed, final.qualification.outcome is qualified, and final.qualification.correct is true. These describe the reported evaluation outcome, not universal scientific validity or publication acceptance.\\\",\n+    \\\"No downstream_study or study.* grounding sources exist. Do not invent a campaign designation, frozen-selection rationale, search-score difference or scored/unscored attempt accounting under that namespace. The selected-method identity is corroborated by result.top_program_01, results/best_program_manifest.json and the available selected source; the final artifact separately records its program-tree digest. Do not claim an independently recomputed tree-hash match.\\\",\n+    \\\"Directly inspected results/ideas/03_checkpoint_weighted_flip_path_exchange/program_1/src/program.py and IMPLEMENTATION.md: the method aggregates sufficient statistics, retains a width-two exact-refitted path generator, and refines a complete nested flip path using screened swaps and replacements. It does not implement provenance-matched deletions or a width-four crossing beam as its defining contribution.\\\",\n+    \\\"The final evidence has Arena and NBA 2011–2015, not evaluated MT-Bench human/judge matching. Treat these as separate condition-specific evidence blocks under one sensitivity question, with a shared estimator/intervention and an NBA home-effect adaptation, not matched datasets or a causal contrast of evaluation designs.\\\",\n+    \\\"The final case-level paired intervals materially constrain the thesis: all Arena baseline contrasts have positive lower endpoints across the recorded seeds, while several NBA contrasts include zero. There is no component ablation bundle, so attribution to exchange alone is unsupported.\\\",\n+    \\\"The current bibliography and provenance contain retrieved metadata, including many irrelevant entries, without full-text reading attestations. This does not block a scientific framing, but it blocks treating those records as an already verified related-work base. Do not cite a record merely because retrieval populated it. No figure assets currently exist.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"method_groups\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Influence-guided exact-refit flip-path exchange\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"proposed\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"The selected method studied in final evidence: frozen-contrast influence calculations, adaptive exact-refitted path construction, bounded complete-path swaps/replacements and a complete incumbent fallback. Explain these as the evaluated bundle, not separately proven sources of gain.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Uniform random outcome flips\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Provides a same-budget unstructured perturbation reference, averaged over the recorded random streams rather than selected after observing performance.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Degree-quartile-matched random flips\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Controls approximately for the degree-sum exposure profile of the actual selected prefixes. Explicitly distinguish coarse quartile matching from exact endpoint, content, question-block or cross-design matching.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Smallest absolute matchup-margin flips\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Tests whether a simple fitted-closeness rule explains the observed disruption without guided complete-path selection.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Independent refit and integrity diagnostics\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"supporting\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Explain no-op, rotated-priority, reset-state and explicitly synthetic constant-zero controls as integrity checks, not competitive algorithms, architecture ablations or evidence of real historical manipulation.\\\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"results_focus\\\": [\n+    \\\"Primary comparison: show all four methods for all six final cases at each of the three nominal fractions, 0.1%, 0.5% and 1% of all usable observations. Plot categorical budgets without connecting them as an optimization trajectory. Report floor-rounded integer costs, and make clear that only binary outcomes can be flipped while ties remain in fitting and in the denominator.\\\",\n+    \\\"Reader-facing primary metric: pairwise-order disruption, the number of participant-pair order reversals divided by the number of participant pairs, using the fixed participant-index tie order. Its reconstruction from stored original_scores and edited_scores matches every stored candidate_curves value exactly. Larger values mean a more disruptive stress test, not better predictive accuracy or a more accurate leaderboard.\\\",\n+    \\\"Keep the final overall statistic as a compact supporting table: proposed 0.055641534391534395, uniform random 0.00935242200328407, degree-quartile matched 0.011150133225384662, and close-margin 0.007573891625615763. Ground these in their respective final.metric.* sources. Explain equal weights over budgets, seeds and design families, with equal seasons within NBA; do not silently pool observations or let the five seasons outweigh Arena.\\\",\n+    \\\"Essential uncertainty: show recorded paired candidate-minus-baseline intervals by case and seed in the main paper. They summarize budget-averaged disruption under fixed intervention plans, not separately each plotted budget. Arena intervals are positive for all three baselines in all seeds. Several NBA intervals include zero; NBA 2013–2015 include zero for all three baselines in all recorded seeds. Do not replace these with a universal significant-superiority claim.\\\",\n+    \\\"Main limitations must accompany the main results: only 30 grouped bootstrap replicates per final case/seed, no reselection of interventions inside bootstrap, three algorithmic seeds rather than independent datasets, a single crowd panel, unequal graphs and data volumes, a fixed ridge, and omitted temporal/dynamic effects. No new population-level, cross-design causal, temporal-transfer or optimality claim follows.\\\",\n+    \\\"Use graph descriptors and actual flip counts to explain the estimand and comparison regime, not as fitted causal explanations of performance. Final Arena has 64 participants; each final NBA panel has 30. Finite-change influence approximation discrepancy is nonzero and is not a failure of the audited derivative arithmetic by itself.\\\",\n+    \\\"No main-body search chronology, no search-to-final delta, no winner progression, no measured loss assigned to an unscored attempt, and no original-incumbent superiority comparison: a matched final evaluation of the original candidate is absent. Retain the three original final-evidence comparator families above. Search artifacts may document configuration provenance only, clearly labeled as development evidence rather than final replication.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"figure_plan\\\": [\n+    \\\"Early overview: two compact conceptual panels show the fixed comparison graph and legal nested outcome flips, then influence screening, complete-path exchange, exact refits and matched-budget comparison with conditional uncertainty. No invented graph measurements or illustrative empirical ranks.\\\",\n+    \\\"Direct final comparison: three vertically stacked grouped-dot panels, one per nominal edit fraction, each with the six observed cases and four method series. Keep unconnected markers, common metric semantics and a common vertical scale.\\\",\n+    \\\"Paired uncertainty: three vertically stacked forest panels, one per baseline, each with six case categories and three offset seed-specific intervals; include zero explicitly. Label the estimand as budget-averaged fixed-plan paired disruption difference.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"figure_specs\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"sensitivity_overview\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Give immediate glance value for the intervention, the evaluated method bundle and the separation between measured sensitivity and unsupported causal or robustness claims.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"diagram\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"generate-concept-figure\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"intervention_and_evidence\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"none; structural explanation only\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"legal_perturbation_and_evaluation\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected ICLR article template and paper.sty: one 5.5-inch text column and 9-inch text height, not two conference columns. Two side-by-side sparse panels fit at full text width; target 1.6–1.9 inches high excluding caption, with final labels at least 9 pt. Place on page 1 or 2. A half-width placement would make the mechanism labels unnecessarily small.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 6,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"content_spec\\\": \\\"Panel 1: fixed observed pairwise-comparison graph, tied observations retained/uneditable, distinct nested binary flips at fixed costs, and unchanged estimator. Panel 2: influence screening plus exact-refitted path selection/exchange, three matched-budget baseline families, paired grouped resampling conditional on fixed plans. Show Arena and NBA as unequal evidence blocks; no causal arrow between them. The diagram depicts methodological structure, not a measured attack example. Corroborate mechanism labels against the selected program and public task contract.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"final_disruption_comparison\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Show all final method comparisons without hiding case heterogeneity behind an overall mean or presenting budget responses as search dynamics.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"grouped_dot\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"matplotlib\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"case\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"pairwise-order disruption\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"nominal_edit_fraction\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"Use the inspected single-column 5.5-inch text width, with three vertical panels rather than three narrow horizontal plots. Six abbreviated case labels and four offset method markers remain readable at 8–9 pt; target 3.7–4.2 inches total height excluding caption. One shared legend and common axis semantics avoid repetition. This is full text width, not a two-column figure* assumption.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 3,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 6,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 1,\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"content_spec\\\": \\\"Read candidate_curves, baseline_curves and counts for arena and nba-2011 through nba-2015. Show the mean of the three recorded algorithmic seeds as a descriptive summary computed only from those recorded values; preserve individual seed values in the supplement, do not invent error bars, and do not call seeds independent datasets. State explicitly that uncertainty is in the separate paired-interval figure. Use a main-text cost table to report actual integer counts instead of squeezing them into every marker label.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"paired_effect_uncertainty\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Keep the strongest positive and inconclusive evidence together and prevent aggregate disruption from being mistaken for universal superiority.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"forest\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"matplotlib\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"case\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"budget-averaged fixed-plan paired disruption difference\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"baseline_family\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"At the inspected 5.5-inch single-column width, three vertically stacked baseline panels allow six case rows and three modestly offset seed intervals per row without shrinking labels. Target 4.6–5.2 inches high excluding caption, 8–9 pt case labels and a clear zero reference. Do not shrink this to half width or pack three forest panels horizontally.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 3,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 6,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 3,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 1,\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"content_spec\\\": \\\"Use paired_intervals for each seed and case exactly as recorded. Display endpoints as interval segments, not fabricated centers or inferred confidence intervals for the original-sample point estimate. If adding point markers, derive the bootstrap mean paired effect from the corresponding bootstrap[].paired entries and label that statistic explicitly; do not silently substitute the unresampled effect. Prefer intervals alone to avoid this ambiguity. Use comparator color consistently across panels and seed-specific line styles/offsets. Do not pool seeds, construct a design-family confidence interval, or imply simultaneous/multiplicity-adjusted coverage.\\\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"supplementary_plan\\\": {\n+    \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Add substantive implementation, complete recorded evidence and reproducibility detail after the references, while keeping all six-case comparisons, essential uncertainty and scope restrictions in the main paper. Include only analyses already supported by the current evidence; later authoritative appendix-ranked analyses may be added without changing this strategy.\\\",\n+    \\\"planned_subsections\\\": [\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Complete Case, Budget and Seed Results\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Tables of candidate_curves, all baseline_curves, counts, paired_intervals and graph descriptors for every final case/seed. Preserve intervals that include zero and the repeated nature of algorithmic seeds. Include recorded original/edited rank intervals where useful, without inventing per-budget intervals absent from the evidence.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Influence Arithmetic and Finite-Change Diagnostics\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Explain unit-outcome derivatives versus binary-flip signed shifts, the frozen original Hessian and independent exact refits, using the selected program and public contract as method documentation. Tabulate recorded influence_errors by case/budget and method_audit and control outcomes. The overall finite-change discrepancy is 0.14315313656317594; do not interpret it as a rate of invalid results or prove hidden implementation internals from a passing audit.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.metric.influence_error\\\", \\\"final.metric.control_error\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Nested Flip-Path Construction and Reproducibility\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Document the centered sum-loss ridge-1 objective, sufficient-statistic representation, width-two generator, selected-position swaps, unused-row replacements, affected-prefix caching, strict complete-path acceptance and incumbent fallback from the available selected source. Report source-declared bounds as settings, not measured usage: 128 optional proposals, 72 additional converged fits at dimension at most 64 and 24 otherwise, and a two-second soft optional-search deadline. An ongoing fit is not interrupted; load-dependent truncation limits bitwise reproducibility. Include the recorded final seeds, observable durations, program-tree digest and exact existing dependency/data-acquisition files. Do not invent per-method runtimes or claim reproduction has been rerun. Final evidence anchors the evaluated bundle; implementation details are corroborated by the named program and public contract, not inferred from metric values.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.qualification.status\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Data Provenance and Scope of Comparability\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Use task/resources/final/manifest.json and task/prepare_data.py as existing provenance documentation alongside the final graph/count evidence: Arena normalized document-connected groups, unique NBA games, reciprocal-row handling, content-disjoint partition policy, source snapshots/checksums and license records where actually available. Distinguish a manifest assertion from an independently rerun verification. Explain fractional ties, NBA home effects, season-specific fitting and unequal graph coverage. No MT-Bench, expert/judge or block-deletion results can be added.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Evaluation Outcome and Claim Boundaries\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Record the completed and qualified final evaluation using final.qualification.*, separately from point estimates and publication judgment. Explain that numerical audits and four controls have limited scope, that candidate diagnostics are marked unverified, and that no comparative-superiority gate is implied. Do not invent absent gate diagnostics. If later authoritative evidence reports failed qualification, update the main claims, review, audit and revisions together; do not silently retain a qualified characterization.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.qualification.status\\\", \\\"final.qualification.outcome\\\", \\\"final.qualification.correct\\\", \\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"LLM Usage\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Disclose the documented assistance with ideation, candidate-source preparation, reference-query planning and paper framing/writing. Separate static preparation statements from actual recorded evaluator execution. Use source paths and assistant logs as provenance, without claiming any undocumented model-generated judgments of the empirical data, prohibited-source access, or literature reading. Redact identifying paths and keep the submission anonymous.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"result.top_program_01\\\", \\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  },\n+  \\\"forbidden_headings\\\": [\n+    \\\"Search Progression\\\",\n+    \\\"Campaign Timeline\\\",\n+    \\\"Milestones\\\",\n+    \\\"First Valid Result\\\",\n+    \\\"Experiment A / Experiment B\\\",\n+    \\\"Phase 1 / Phase 2\\\",\n+    \\\"Round-by-Round Improvements\\\",\n+    \\\"From Failure to Winner\\\",\n+    \\\"Architecture Ablations\\\",\n+    \\\"Matched MT-Bench Deletion Results\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"forbidden_phrases\\\": [\n+    \\\"first valid result\\\",\n+    \\\"we then tried\\\",\n+    \\\"subsequent improvements\\\",\n+    \\\"next-best\\\",\n+    \\\"later variants\\\",\n+    \\\"winning iteration\\\",\n+    \\\"correctness rate\\\",\n+    \\\"correct and eligible\\\",\n+    \\\"eligible\\\",\n+    \\\"worker_01\\\",\n+    \\\"worker_02\\\",\n+    \\\"combined_score\\\",\n+    \\\"rubric\\\",\n+    \\\"state-of-the-art leaderboard attack\\\",\n+    \\\"certified minimum manipulation budget\\\",\n+    \\\"exactly exposure-matched\\\",\n+    \\\"all NBA comparisons are significant\\\",\n+    \\\"sports evaluation is causally more robust\\\",\n+    \\\"the exchange component explains the gain\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"notes_for_writer\\\": [\n+    \\\"Organize thesis-first: Introduction; Related Work; Ranking Sensitivity and Perturbation Model; Influence-Guided Exact-Refit Stress Testing; Evaluation Design; Results and Conditional Uncertainty; Discussion and Limitations; Conclusion. Arena and NBA are evidence blocks for one question, not two chronologically ordered experiments.\\\",\n+    \\\"Plan approximately 8.5 body pages including figures and captions: abstract/introduction 1.2, related work 0.6, estimand/model 1.0, method 1.4, evaluation design 1.1, results 2.1, discussion/limitations 0.9, conclusion 0.2. These are layout targets, not measured results. The venue permits 8–9 pages excluding references, with an 8-page body valid only if its final page is at least 75% full. Spend space on equations, clear comparison design, graph/count context, complete uncertainty and limitations, not a search log, speculative theory or decorative material. Rebalance within the cap rather than padding.\\\",\n+    \\\"Inspected .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.tex and paper.sty: article is single-column, textwidth 5.5 inches and textheight 9 inches on letter paper. There is no separate half-page conference column; column width equals full text width. All three required figures therefore use ordinary full-text-width figures. Keep practical final-size font targets rather than shrinking dense assets.\\\",\n+    \\\"The supplied scaffold enables final-copy mode and contains an author string: remove that mode and author identity for the anonymous ICLR 2026 submission, omit affiliations, acknowledgements and funding, and retain any orchestrator-owned watermark block unchanged. Do not claim official latest-template provenance has been independently verified merely because the supplied style is available; document that provenance at the writing/compilation stage. The task contract mentions a different venue, but the current explicit ICLR 2026 venue brief governs this strategy.\\\",\n+    \\\"State the model explicitly: sum of logistic losses plus one-half the squared parameter norm, participant scores centered, optional NBA home covariate regularized with the same fixed coefficient. Ties contribute fractional outcomes but are uneditable. Nominal costs use all usable rows; report exact floor-rounded costs alongside the nominal fractions. Distinguish method internal displacement-first lexicographic selection from the reader-facing inversion-fraction endpoint; they are not identical objectives.\\\",\n+    \\\"Use final.metric.* and final.evidence.episodes for final quantitative claims, and final.qualification.* only for qualification facts. The actual outcome here is qualified, not not_qualified. Absence of downstream_study does not invalidate the independent completed final evaluation. Preserve this separation in later drafting, review, audit and revision. Unknown gate causes remain unknown; neither positive metrics nor publication eligibility override an adverse outcome in other runs.\\\",\n+    \\\"Private-only provenance context: selection corroboration comes from result.top_program_01 and the best-program manifest, while the final program-tree digest is recorded independently. No study.* namespace is supplied; omit unsupported selection differences and attempt-count claims rather than synthesizing aliases. Do not compare the earlier candidate as a final baseline or label differing search submissions as controlled ablations.\\\",\n+    \\\"The main paper must say that these are feasible observed-outcome counterfactual changes, not evidence of historical vote rigging, population preference change or attacker access in deployed systems. Finding a disruptive path gives an attainable sensitivity witness, not an optimal attack, a lower bound on necessary changes, or a certificate of robustness.\\\",\n+    \\\"Uncertainty is conditional on fixed selected interventions and fixed panels. Thirty resamples give coarse percentile endpoints; three seeds are not three independent datasets; no multiple-comparison correction or adaptive-reselection uncertainty is established. Keep the inconclusive NBA evidence in the main text and figure, not only in the supplement.\\\",\n+    \\\"Do not invent component ablations, alternative ridge sweeps, deletion studies, matched human/judge data, successful target reversals, runtime speedups, unseen-model or temporal generalization, or architectures. A mechanistic description of exchange is supported by code, but attributing the observed advantage specifically to exchange is not supported by a controlled final ablation.\\\",\n+    \\\"Quantitative plots must be regenerated from recorded arrays by saved scripts and exported as vector PDF plus PNG at 300 DPI; LaTeX must reference the PDF whenever it exists. Use the same four method colors throughout, colorblind-safe markers, abbreviated case labels and shared legends. Derived seed means must be explicitly labeled summaries of the recorded values, never new experimental observations.\\\",\n+    \\\"Plan exactly one generate-concept-figure overview. The orchestrator owns rendering; the writer only wires the figure and its manifest/prompt-log entries according to the skill. If an editable vector export yields a PDF, use that PDF in LaTeX; otherwise require the full-width PNG to be regenerated at at least 2400 pixels wide. Column-only raster assets elsewhere require at least 1200 pixels. Never upscale a raster, fabricate diagram measurements, or invoke the image workflow during this strategy stage.\\\",\n+    \\\"After references, use clearpage, bibliography, clearpage, appendix, and a substantive Supplementary Information section. Include the separate LLM Usage section there. Keep essential baselines, uncertainty and limitations in the main body. Later authoritative appendix-ranked analyses belong in Supplementary Information without retroactively changing this strategy.\\\",\n+    \\\"Safe related work remains a writing prerequisite: the current bibliography is not a verified reading list. Most retrieval results are irrelevant and metadata records alone do not establish that an original was read. Only use admissible relevant originals actually read and citation keys synchronized with the supplied BibTeX/provenance; if needed, repair bibliography grounding in the appropriate later stage. Do not fill space with unrelated retrieved works or claim comprehensive novelty. Do not infer the prohibited work's identity, use citation expansion, or access uncertain related pages; stop and log any accidental encounter without continuing.\\\",\n+    \\\"Only strategy outputs are created in this stage: no paper.tex, claims_grounding.json, new scientific experiments or final-paper validation. Validate JSON shape, source-ID resolution, figure budgets and memo agreement only. No required empirical result is deferred to a hypothetical future experiment.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"failure_reason\\\": \\\"\\\"\n+}\n*** Add File: paper_strategy.md\n+# Paper Framing Strategy\n+\n+**Status:** ready for a grounded standalone-paper plan, not a claim of publication readiness.  \n+**Family:** \"'`paper_standalone`, using `write-paper-standalone`.  \n+**Provisional title:** *Exact-Refit Stress Tests for Bradley–Terry Rankings*.  \n+**Venue:** anonymous ICLR 2026 submission; 8–9 body pages excluding references.\n+\n+## Central Question and Thesis\n+\n+**Question.** How much can small, matched-budget binary-outcome changes disrupt fitted Bradley–Terry orderings on the observed Arena and NBA panels, and how consistently do exact-refitted guided interventions exceed simple controls?\n+\n+**Thesis.** On these fixed panels, influence-guided flip-path exchange produces larger budget-averaged pairwise-order disruption point estimates than three matched-budget baselines. Conditional bootstrap evidence supports a clearer advantage on Arena than across NBA seasons. This is an empirical sensitivity study, not a proof of an optimal attack, population generalization or a causal difference between evaluation designs.\n+\n+This story uses one shared estimator/intervention with condition-specific evidence blocks: a crowdsourced Arena panel and season-specific sports panels. They are neither matched datasets nor a controlled experiment on evaluation design. NBA'\"'s home-effect adaptation belongs in the model description, not a separate method family.\n+\n+## Evidence and Qualification Audit\n+\n+Read \"'`paper_data.json.final_evaluation` independently of other study metadata. Its reported status is completed, outcome qualified and correctness flag true, grounded respectively in `final.qualification.status`, `final.qualification.outcome` and `final.qualification.correct`. Do not turn these reported outcomes into publication approval, universal validity or comparative superiority. Candidate diagnostic trust is explicitly unverified; use recorded independent refit/audit evidence only within its documented scope.\n+\n+There is no `downstream_study` or `study.*` source namespace. Do not fabricate a campaign classification, attempt accounting or search-score differences under that namespace. The available selected source and `results/best_program_manifest.json` corroborate the identity in `result.top_program_01`; the final record separately supplies a program-tree digest. No independent recomputation of that tree digest is claimed. Keep development provenance separate from final results, and omit an original-candidate performance comparison because no matched final evaluation of that comparator is supplied.\n+\n+The completed final evaluation is usable even without downstream-study metadata. In another run, a completed but unqualified outcome would require explicit failed-qualification disclosure throughout drafting, review, audit and revision; neither retained metrics nor publication eligibility could erase it. Here the actual reported outcome is qualified. Never invent absent gate diagnostics or attribute an unknown failure to performance, validity or adaptivity.\n+\n+### Decisive Grounded Results\n+\n+- `final.evidence.episodes` contains three final seeds, 401, 503 and 607, each with Arena and NBA 2011–2015. These are algorithmic seeds, not independent datasets.\n+- Primary endpoint: participant-pair ordering reversals divided by the number of participant pairs, with the fixed participant-index tie rule. Reconstructing it from stored original and edited scores exactly reproduces every stored candidate endpoint. Larger values mean stronger disruption, not improved ranking accuracy.\n+- Nominal fractions are 0.1%, 0.5% and 1% of all usable rows, floored to integers. Ties remain in fitting and in the denominator but cannot be flipped. Arena costs are 43, 216 and 432 flips; NBA 2012 costs are 1, 5 and 10; other final NBA seasons use 1, 6 and 13. Report counts alongside nominal fractions.\n+- Final overall disruption values are 0.055641534391534395 for the proposed bundle, 0.00935242200328407 for uniform random, 0.011150133225384662 for degree-quartile matched, and 0.007573891625615763 for close-margin flips. Source each from the corresponding `final.metric.*` entry, not from search results.\n+- Explain the weighting: equal budgets and seeds within case, equal NBA seasons within the sports family, and equal weight for the two design families. Do not pool rows or overweight NBA because it has five panels.\n+- Arena'\"'s paired intervals have positive lower endpoints against all three baselines in all recorded seeds. Multiple NBA intervals include zero; NBA 2013–2015 do so for all three baselines across all seeds. This uncertainty is essential main-body evidence, not supplemental fine print.\n+- These intervals concern budget-averaged disruption under fixed intervention plans, not each individual budget point. They use 30 grouped bootstrap replicates per final case/seed. No reselection, seed pooling, design-family confidence interval, multiplicity adjustment or independent-population replication is established.\n+- Final graphs have 64 Arena participants and 30 in each NBA season. Graph coverage, finite-change influence discrepancies and fixed regularization constrain interpretation. Do not fit causal explanations to those descriptors.\n+\n+## Explicit Framing Decision\n+\n+There is no edit-mode context or prior manuscript: \"'`previous_paper/`, `aggregated/` and `extra_tasks/` are absent. The JSON status `prior_paper_story_status: rejected` rejects the earlier prospective story, not an unseen manuscript.\n+\n+| Candidate framing | Decision and grounded reason |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| Preserve exposure-matched MT-Bench block deletion with local updates | Reject: evaluated outcomes are binary flips on Arena/NBA, not question-block deletions or matched human/judge contrasts. |\n+| Broaden to a general deletion/flip robustness family | Reject as the thesis: the shared family would contain unmeasured interventions and unavailable matching. |\n+| Recenter on attainable finite-flip sensitivity with exact refits | Select: directly supported by final case/budget/baseline evidence and uncertainty, with two real evaluation designs. |\n+| Tell a search-winner or component-improvement story | Reject: search order is not the scientific question, and no controlled component-ablation bundle exists. |\n+\n+Direct inspection of the selected `program.py` and `IMPLEMENTATION.md` supports sufficient-statistic aggregation, a width-two exact-refitted path generator, complete-path swaps/replacements and fallback. Do not import the different width-four branch as the selected mechanism. The intervention interface supplies no provenance-aware deletion or cross-design matching. No old title or figure plan is retained by inertia.\n+\n+## Narrow Method Set\n+\n+1. **Proposed:** influence-guided exact-refit flip-path exchange, treated as one evaluated bundle. Explain its original-Hessian screening, nested paths, exact-refitted comparisons, affected-prefix caching and complete incumbent fallback. Do not attribute the aggregate advantage specifically to exchange without an ablation.\n+2. **Baseline:** uniform random binary-outcome flips, using the recorded stream averages.\n+3. **Baseline:** degree-sum-quartile-matched random flips, conditional on the actual selected prefixes. This is approximate exposure control, not exact endpoint/content matching.\n+4. **Baseline:** smallest absolute fitted matchup-margin flips.\n+5. **Supporting diagnostics only:** independent refits and no-op, rotated-priority, reset and explicitly synthetic constant-zero checks. These are not additional competitive algorithms or architectural ablations.\n+\n+Define the fixed model: summed logistic losses plus one-half the squared parameter norm, centered participant scores and an optional regularized NBA home coefficient. Preserve ridge 1 and the fixed tie rule. Distinguish the method'\"'s displacement-first lexicographic internal objective from the inversion-fraction endpoint. A mathematically correct local derivative does not imply accurate finite-change ranking predictions; exact refits determine measured endpoints.\n+\n+## Required Figures and Readability Budgets\n+\n+The inspected ICLR template uses \"'`article`; `paper.sty` sets a **single 5.5-inch text column and 9-inch text height**. Thus ordinary column width equals full text width. There is no two-column `figure*` geometry to borrow, and half-width figures would unnecessarily constrain labels. All required figures use the full 5.5-inch text width. Heights below exclude captions.\n+\n+### 1. `sensitivity_overview`: Early Conceptual Overview\n+\n+- **Generator:** `generate-concept-figure`, exactly once in the plan; rendering belongs to the orchestrator, not this strategy stage.\n+- **Placement:** page 1 or 2; full text width; approximately 1.6–1.9 inches high; final labels at least 9 pt.\n+- **Content:** two sparse side-by-side panels. The first defines fixed observed comparisons, uneditable ties and legal nested flips. The second relates influence screening, complete-path selection/exchange, independent exact refits, three matched-budget baselines and fixed-plan grouped uncertainty. Arena and NBA are unequal evidence blocks, not causally linked designs.\n+- **Budget:** at most two panels, two per row, six conceptual categories and four semantic series per panel. No invented empirical graph or rank-change example, decorative architecture or measured values.\n+- **Grounding:** `final.evidence.episodes`, with mechanism labels corroborated by the selected implementation and public task contract.\n+\n+### 2. `final_disruption_comparison`: All Cases and Budgets\n+\n+- **Generator:** matplotlib; grouped dots, not connected trajectories.\n+- **Placement:** full text width; three vertically stacked panels; approximately 3.7–4.2 inches high, 8–9 pt labels.\n+- **Content:** one panel per nominal fraction; six case categories; four method series. Use a common metric scale and one shared legend. Mark descriptive means of the three recorded seeds; put individual values in the supplement and actual integer costs in a main-text table.\n+- **Budget:** at most three panels, one per row, six categories and four series per panel. No invented error bars or interpretation of seeds as datasets; the next figure supplies paired uncertainty.\n+- **Grounding:** stored `candidate_curves`, `baseline_curves` and `counts` under `final.evidence.episodes`. Seed means are transparent arithmetic summaries of recorded values, not new observations.\n+\n+### 3. `paired_effect_uncertainty`: Conditional Effects and Null-Compatible Cases\n+\n+- **Generator:** matplotlib; forest plot with a clear zero reference.\n+- **Placement:** full text width; three vertical baseline panels; approximately 4.6–5.2 inches high, 8–9 pt labels. Do not squeeze three forest panels horizontally or shrink this to half width.\n+- **Content:** six cases per panel; three modestly offset seed-specific intervals per case. Use recorded budget-averaged `paired_intervals` exactly. Keep Arena'\"'s clearer advantage beside NBA's inconclusive comparisons.\n+- **Budget:** at most three panels, one per row, six categories and three seed series per panel.\n+- **Statistical labeling:** show interval segments without fabricated centers. If a point marker is necessary, compute and label the mean of the corresponding recorded bootstrap paired effects, rather than silently inserting the original-sample effect or interval midpoint. Do not pool seeds or claim simultaneous coverage.\n+- **Grounding:** \"'`final.evidence.episodes`. Budget-specific point comparisons and budget-averaged intervals are distinct estimands and must be labeled accordingly.\n+\n+### Export Contract\n+\n+Save plotting scripts and input mappings. Export quantitative figures as vector PDF and PNG at 300 DPI; include the PDF in LaTeX whenever available. Keep method colors and markers consistent and colorblind-safe. For the concept figure, preserve editable source and use a vector PDF if available; otherwise regenerate the full-width raster at at least 2400 pixels wide. Other column-only rasters require at least 1200 pixels. Never upscale an existing raster. The writer wires concept-figure manifest/prompt-log entries according to the skill; it does not run the orchestrator-owned pipeline.\n+\n+## Body Layout and Page Use\n+\n+Target approximately **8.5 body pages**, including captions and figures, within the explicit 8–9-page venue budget. An exactly eight-page body must leave its last page at least 75% full. Use scientific depth, not padding:\n+\n+| Scientific section | Approximate page allocation | Value supplied |\n+| --- | ---: | --- |\n+| Abstract and introduction | 1.2 | Problem, scoped contributions and early overview |\n+| Related work | 0.6 | Relevant actually read methods and positioning, not retrieval filler |\n+| Ranking sensitivity and perturbation model | 1.0 | Estimand, fixed objective, ties, costs and order conventions |\n+| Influence-guided exact-refit stress testing | 1.4 | Bundle, derivative/refit distinction, nested path construction and limits |\n+| Evaluation design | 1.1 | Panel provenance, graph/count table, baselines, weighting and bootstrap |\n+| Results and conditional uncertainty | 2.1 | All-case comparison, final aggregate table, paired intervals and inconclusive cases |\n+| Discussion and limitations | 0.9 | Scope, approximation, adaptive selection, unequal graphs and no causal claims |\n+| Conclusion | 0.2 | Narrow answer to the research question |\n+\n+These are layout targets rather than empirical values. Rebalance within the cap; do not invent theory, sweeps, baselines or chronology to reach it. The substantive model/protocol explanation and uncertainty analysis justify the space even without component ablations.\n+\n+The supplied template scaffold includes final-copy mode and an author identity. The writer must remove both for anonymous review, omit affiliations/acknowledgements/funding, avoid identifying links and preserve the orchestrator-owned watermark block unchanged. The current ICLR brief governs venue choice despite older task-contract venue language. Inspect and document official template provenance later rather than claiming the supplied style proves latest-edition compliance now.\n+\n+## Supplementary Information After References\n+\n+Purpose: provide complete existing evidence and reproducibility depth without hiding evidence essential to the thesis. Use `clearpage`, bibliography, `clearpage`, appendix and a substantive `Supplementary Information` section in the final paper. Route later authoritative appendix-ranked analyses here without retroactively revising this strategy.\n+\n+1. **Complete Case, Budget and Seed Results.** All candidate/baseline endpoints, integer counts, intervals and graph descriptors, including null-compatible cases. Use recorded rank intervals where useful without manufacturing absent budget-specific uncertainty. Source: `final.evidence.episodes`.\n+2. **Influence Arithmetic and Finite-Change Diagnostics.** Distinguish unit derivatives, signed flip shifts and nonlinear discrepancies; tabulate recorded errors, method audits and control outcomes. The recorded overall discrepancy is 0.14315313656317594, not an invalidity rate. Sources: `final.evidence.episodes`, `final.metric.influence_error`, `final.metric.control_error`; corroborate method equations with code and the public contract.\n+3. **Nested Flip-Path Construction and Reproducibility.** Document the available selected code'\"'s width-two generator, swaps/replacements, cache and fallback. Source-declared optional limits are 128 proposals, 72 added converged fits at dimension at most 64 and 24 otherwise, plus a two-second soft deadline; these are not measured usage or a hard interruption bound. Include recorded seeds/durations/digest and existing dependency/acquisition files, never invented per-method runtimes or claims of a fresh reproduction. Sources: \"'`final.evidence.episodes`, `final.qualification.status`, corroborated by the explicitly named implementation.\n+4. **Data Provenance and Scope of Comparability.** Explain normalized Arena document groups, unique NBA games, reciprocal-row handling, partition policy, ties, home effects, season-specific fitting and unequal coverage. Use `task/resources/final/manifest.json` and `task/prepare_data.py` as available documentation, distinguishing manifest assertions from independently rerun checks. Anchor empirical graph/count evidence to `final.evidence.episodes`; do not invent missing licenses/checksums or add MT-Bench results.\n+5. **Evaluation Outcome and Claim Boundaries.** Separate reported completed/qualified status, numerical audits, unverified candidate diagnostics and publication judgment. Preserve all limitations and unknown diagnostics in review/audit/revision. Sources: `final.qualification.status`, `final.qualification.outcome`, `final.qualification.correct`, `final.evidence.episodes`.\n+6. **LLM Usage.** A separate disclosure section describing documented ideation, code preparation, reference planning, framing and writing assistance. Distinguish static preparation from recorded evaluator execution; omit unsupported literature-reading or empirical-judging claims. Use available assistant logs, `result.top_program_01` and `final.evidence.episodes` for traceability; redact identifying paths.\n+\n+Source IDs above are existing registered anchors; file paths supply additional documentary support rather than pretending that metric entries independently prove source-code internals or provenance checks.\n+\n+## Claims, References and Wording Guardrails\n+\n+Do not infer historical misconduct, attacker access, global optimality, a minimum required corruption budget, population preference change, unseen-model performance or temporal generalization. An attainable disruption is a sensitivity witness, not a robustness certificate. Approximate exposure control does not make the two data designs comparable in a causal sense. No final component ablations, ridge sweeps, deletions or matched human/judge analyses exist.\n+\n+The existing bibliography is a retrieval output, not an already verified reading list: provenance is metadata-only and many entries are irrelevant. Related work must use admissible relevant originals actually read, with synchronized BibTeX/provenance keys. Do not cite irrelevant records to fill space, claim comprehensive novelty, perform citation expansion, infer the prohibited study'\"'s identity or access uncertain related pages. If forbidden material is encountered accidentally, stop and record location and amount read. No such encounter is claimed in this framing stage.\n+\n+**Forbidden headings:** Search Progression; Campaign Timeline; Milestones; First Valid Result; Experiment A / Experiment B; Phase 1 / Phase 2; Round-by-Round Improvements; From Failure to Winner; Architecture Ablations; Matched MT-Bench Deletion Results.\n+\n+**Forbidden visible phrases:** first valid result; we then tried; subsequent improvements; next-best; later variants; winning iteration; correctness rate; correct and eligible; eligible; worker_01; worker_02; combined_score; rubric; state-of-the-art leaderboard attack; certified minimum manipulation budget; exactly exposure-matched; all NBA comparisons are significant; sports evaluation is causally more robust; the exchange component explains the gain. Internal identifiers in this strategy are private provenance only, not recommendations for reader-facing labels.\n+\n+## Handoff and Stage Limits\n+\n+Implement the required figures first, preserve their readability budgets, and keep both the strong and inconclusive evidence visible. Quantitative final claims use \"'`final.metric.*` or `final.evidence.episodes`; qualification facts use `final.qualification.*`. Search provenance is not final replication and unscored work is not a measured loss.\n+\n+This stage produces only the strategy memo and JSON plus append-only memory updates. It does not draft `paper.tex`, create `claims_grounding.json`, run candidate/evaluator experiments, generate figures or perform final-paper validation. Check strategy JSON structure, source-ID resolution, figure budgets and memo consistency only. No necessary empirical result is deferred to a hypothetical later experiment.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"apply_patch() { python -c 'import pathlib,sys\nlines=sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\nassert lines[0]==\\\"*** Begin Patch\\\" and lines[-1]==\\\"*** End Patch\\\"\nposition=1\nwhile position<len(lines)-1:\n    assert lines[position].startswith(\\\"*** Add File: \\\"), \\\"Only new-file patches are supported\\\"\n    target=pathlib.Path(lines[position].split(\\\": \\\",1)[1]); position+=1; content=[]\n    while position<len(lines)-1 and not lines[position].startswith(\\\"*** Add File: \\\"):\n        assert lines[position].startswith(\\\"+\\\"); content.append(lines[position][1:]); position+=1\n    with target.open(\\\"x\\\",encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as output: output.write(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(content)+\\\"\\\\n\\\")\n    print(\\\"Added\\\",target)\n'; }\napply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: paper_strategy.json\n+{\n+  \\\"status\\\": \\\"ready\\\",\n+  \\\"selected_prompt_family\\\": \\\"paper_standalone\\\",\n+  \\\"recommended_title\\\": \\\"Exact-Refit Stress Tests for Bradley–Terry Rankings\\\",\n+  \\\"central_question\\\": \\\"How much can small, matched-budget binary-outcome changes disrupt fitted Bradley–Terry orderings on the observed Arena and NBA panels, and how consistently do exact-refitted guided interventions exceed simple controls?\\\",\n+  \\\"central_thesis\\\": \\\"On the fixed Arena and NBA panels, influence-guided flip-path exchange yields larger budget-averaged pairwise-order disruption point estimates than three matched-budget baselines, but fixed-plan bootstrap evidence supports a clearer advantage on Arena than across NBA seasons.\\\",\n+  \\\"narrative_rationale\\\": \\\"The strongest evidence is the completed final evaluation of one selected outcome-flip method on two real evaluation designs, with independently refitted endpoints, three baselines, graph summaries and paired uncertainty. The paper should study attainable finite-perturbation sensitivity, not tell an improvement story or claim a certified robustness radius. The positive Arena contrasts and inconclusive sports contrasts jointly support a useful, bounded empirical-methodology study. The aggregate difference is not proof of a particular component's contribution or of a causal evaluation-design effect. Readiness here means a coherent framing is supported, not that publication, novelty or manuscript validation has been established.\\\",\n+  \\\"prior_paper_story_status\\\": \\\"rejected\\\",\n+  \\\"edit_framing_decision\\\": \\\"This is not edit mode: no resolved edit-context files, previous_paper manuscript, aggregated directory or extra_tasks directory is present. There is no prior manuscript story to preserve. The rejected alternative is the prospective exposure-matched MT-Bench block-deletion story recorded in planning, not an existing paper. Reject it as the main story because the implemented and evaluated intervention is anonymous binary-outcome flipping on Arena and NBA. Compare alternatives explicitly: local preservation of the prospective story lacks evaluated deletions and matching; broadening to a shared deletion/flip method would exceed the evidence; recentering on the evaluated finite-flip sensitivity question is supported. No previous title or figure plan is inherited.\\\",\n+  \\\"staged_input_impact\\\": [\n+    \\\"paper_data.json.final_evaluation was read independently: final.qualification.status is completed, final.qualification.outcome is qualified, and final.qualification.correct is true. These describe the reported evaluation outcome, not universal scientific validity or publication acceptance.\\\",\n+    \\\"No downstream_study or study.* grounding sources exist. Do not invent a campaign designation, frozen-selection rationale, search-score difference or scored/unscored attempt accounting under that namespace. The selected-method identity is corroborated by result.top_program_01, results/best_program_manifest.json and the available selected source; the final artifact separately records its program-tree digest. Do not claim an independently recomputed tree-hash match.\\\",\n+    \\\"Directly inspected results/ideas/03_checkpoint_weighted_flip_path_exchange/program_1/src/program.py and IMPLEMENTATION.md: the method aggregates sufficient statistics, retains a width-two exact-refitted path generator, and refines a complete nested flip path using screened swaps and replacements. It does not implement provenance-matched deletions or a width-four crossing beam as its defining contribution.\\\",\n+    \\\"The final evidence has Arena and NBA 2011–2015, not evaluated MT-Bench human/judge matching. Treat these as separate condition-specific evidence blocks under one sensitivity question, with a shared estimator/intervention and an NBA home-effect adaptation, not matched datasets or a causal contrast of evaluation designs.\\\",\n+    \\\"The final case-level paired intervals materially constrain the thesis: all Arena baseline contrasts have positive lower endpoints across the recorded seeds, while several NBA contrasts include zero. There is no component ablation bundle, so attribution to exchange alone is unsupported.\\\",\n+    \\\"The current bibliography and provenance contain retrieved metadata, including many irrelevant entries, without full-text reading attestations. This does not block a scientific framing, but it blocks treating those records as an already verified related-work base. Do not cite a record merely because retrieval populated it. No figure assets currently exist.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"method_groups\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Influence-guided exact-refit flip-path exchange\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"proposed\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"The selected method studied in final evidence: frozen-contrast influence calculations, adaptive exact-refitted path construction, bounded complete-path swaps/replacements and a complete incumbent fallback. Explain these as the evaluated bundle, not separately proven sources of gain.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Uniform random outcome flips\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Provides a same-budget unstructured perturbation reference, averaged over the recorded random streams rather than selected after observing performance.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Degree-quartile-matched random flips\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Controls approximately for the degree-sum exposure profile of the actual selected prefixes. Explicitly distinguish coarse quartile matching from exact endpoint, content, question-block or cross-design matching.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Smallest absolute matchup-margin flips\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"baseline\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Tests whether a simple fitted-closeness rule explains the observed disruption without guided complete-path selection.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Independent refit and integrity diagnostics\\\",\n+      \\\"role\\\": \\\"supporting\\\",\n+      \\\"include_reason\\\": \\\"Explain no-op, rotated-priority, reset-state and explicitly synthetic constant-zero controls as integrity checks, not competitive algorithms, architecture ablations or evidence of real historical manipulation.\\\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"results_focus\\\": [\n+    \\\"Primary comparison: show all four methods for all six final cases at each of the three nominal fractions, 0.1%, 0.5% and 1% of all usable observations. Plot categorical budgets without connecting them as an optimization trajectory. Report floor-rounded integer costs, and make clear that only binary outcomes can be flipped while ties remain in fitting and in the denominator.\\\",\n+    \\\"Reader-facing primary metric: pairwise-order disruption, the number of participant-pair order reversals divided by the number of participant pairs, using the fixed participant-index tie order. Its reconstruction from stored original_scores and edited_scores matches every stored candidate_curves value exactly. Larger values mean a more disruptive stress test, not better predictive accuracy or a more accurate leaderboard.\\\",\n+    \\\"Keep the final overall statistic as a compact supporting table: proposed 0.055641534391534395, uniform random 0.00935242200328407, degree-quartile matched 0.011150133225384662, and close-margin 0.007573891625615763. Ground these in their respective final.metric.* sources. Explain equal weights over budgets, seeds and design families, with equal seasons within NBA; do not silently pool observations or let the five seasons outweigh Arena.\\\",\n+    \\\"Essential uncertainty: show recorded paired candidate-minus-baseline intervals by case and seed in the main paper. They summarize budget-averaged disruption under fixed intervention plans, not separately each plotted budget. Arena intervals are positive for all three baselines in all seeds. Several NBA intervals include zero; NBA 2013–2015 include zero for all three baselines in all recorded seeds. Do not replace these with a universal significant-superiority claim.\\\",\n+    \\\"Main limitations must accompany the main results: only 30 grouped bootstrap replicates per final case/seed, no reselection of interventions inside bootstrap, three algorithmic seeds rather than independent datasets, a single crowd panel, unequal graphs and data volumes, a fixed ridge, and omitted temporal/dynamic effects. No new population-level, cross-design causal, temporal-transfer or optimality claim follows.\\\",\n+    \\\"Use graph descriptors and actual flip counts to explain the estimand and comparison regime, not as fitted causal explanations of performance. Final Arena has 64 participants; each final NBA panel has 30. Finite-change influence approximation discrepancy is nonzero and is not a failure of the audited derivative arithmetic by itself.\\\",\n+    \\\"No main-body search chronology, no search-to-final delta, no winner progression, no measured loss assigned to an unscored attempt, and no original-incumbent superiority comparison: a matched final evaluation of the original candidate is absent. Retain the three original final-evidence comparator families above. Search artifacts may document configuration provenance only, clearly labeled as development evidence rather than final replication.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"figure_plan\\\": [\n+    \\\"Early overview: two compact conceptual panels show the fixed comparison graph and legal nested outcome flips, then influence screening, complete-path exchange, exact refits and matched-budget comparison with conditional uncertainty. No invented graph measurements or illustrative empirical ranks.\\\",\n+    \\\"Direct final comparison: three vertically stacked grouped-dot panels, one per nominal edit fraction, each with the six observed cases and four method series. Keep unconnected markers, common metric semantics and a common vertical scale.\\\",\n+    \\\"Paired uncertainty: three vertically stacked forest panels, one per baseline, each with six case categories and three offset seed-specific intervals; include zero explicitly. Label the estimand as budget-averaged fixed-plan paired disruption difference.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"figure_specs\\\": [\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"sensitivity_overview\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Give immediate glance value for the intervention, the evaluated method bundle and the separation between measured sensitivity and unsupported causal or robustness claims.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"diagram\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"generate-concept-figure\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"intervention_and_evidence\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"none; structural explanation only\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"legal_perturbation_and_evaluation\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"Inspected ICLR article template and paper.sty: one 5.5-inch text column and 9-inch text height, not two conference columns. Two side-by-side sparse panels fit at full text width; target 1.6–1.9 inches high excluding caption, with final labels at least 9 pt. Place on page 1 or 2. A half-width placement would make the mechanism labels unnecessarily small.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 6,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 2,\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"content_spec\\\": \\\"Panel 1: fixed observed pairwise-comparison graph, tied observations retained/uneditable, distinct nested binary flips at fixed costs, and unchanged estimator. Panel 2: influence screening plus exact-refitted path selection/exchange, three matched-budget baseline families, paired grouped resampling conditional on fixed plans. Show Arena and NBA as unequal evidence blocks; no causal arrow between them. The diagram depicts methodological structure, not a measured attack example. Corroborate mechanism labels against the selected program and public task contract.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"final_disruption_comparison\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Show all final method comparisons without hiding case heterogeneity behind an overall mean or presenting budget responses as search dynamics.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"grouped_dot\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"matplotlib\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"case\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"pairwise-order disruption\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"nominal_edit_fraction\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"Use the inspected single-column 5.5-inch text width, with three vertical panels rather than three narrow horizontal plots. Six abbreviated case labels and four offset method markers remain readable at 8–9 pt; target 3.7–4.2 inches total height excluding caption. One shared legend and common axis semantics avoid repetition. This is full text width, not a two-column figure* assumption.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 3,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 6,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 4,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 1,\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"content_spec\\\": \\\"Read candidate_curves, baseline_curves and counts for arena and nba-2011 through nba-2015. Show the mean of the three recorded algorithmic seeds as a descriptive summary computed only from those recorded values; preserve individual seed values in the supplement, do not invent error bars, and do not call seeds independent datasets. State explicitly that uncertainty is in the separate paired-interval figure. Use a main-text cost table to report actual integer counts instead of squeezing them into every marker label.\\\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \\\"figure_id\\\": \\\"paired_effect_uncertainty\\\",\n+      \\\"required\\\": true,\n+      \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Keep the strongest positive and inconclusive evidence together and prevent aggregate disruption from being mistaken for universal superiority.\\\",\n+      \\\"figure_type\\\": \\\"forest\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_generator\\\": \\\"matplotlib\\\",\n+      \\\"group_by\\\": \\\"case\\\",\n+      \\\"metric\\\": \\\"budget-averaged fixed-plan paired disruption difference\\\",\n+      \\\"split_by\\\": \\\"baseline_family\\\",\n+      \\\"preferred_span\\\": \\\"full_width\\\",\n+      \\\"target_width_fraction\\\": 1.0,\n+      \\\"layout_rationale\\\": \\\"At the inspected 5.5-inch single-column width, three vertically stacked baseline panels allow six case rows and three modestly offset seed intervals per row without shrinking labels. Target 4.6–5.2 inches high excluding caption, 8–9 pt case labels and a clear zero reference. Do not shrink this to half width or pack three forest panels horizontally.\\\",\n+      \\\"allow_progression\\\": false,\n+      \\\"max_panels\\\": 3,\n+      \\\"max_categories_per_panel\\\": 6,\n+      \\\"max_series_per_panel\\\": 3,\n+      \\\"max_panels_per_row\\\": 1,\n+      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"],\n+      \\\"content_spec\\\": \\\"Use paired_intervals for each seed and case exactly as recorded. Display endpoints as interval segments, not fabricated centers or inferred confidence intervals for the original-sample point estimate. If adding point markers, derive the bootstrap mean paired effect from the corresponding bootstrap[].paired entries and label that statistic explicitly; do not silently substitute the unresampled effect. Prefer intervals alone to avoid this ambiguity. Use comparator color consistently across panels and seed-specific line styles/offsets. Do not pool seeds, construct a design-family confidence interval, or imply simultaneous/multiplicity-adjusted coverage.\\\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \\\"supplementary_plan\\\": {\n+    \\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Add substantive implementation, complete recorded evidence and reproducibility detail after the references, while keeping all six-case comparisons, essential uncertainty and scope restrictions in the main paper. Include only analyses already supported by the current evidence; later authoritative appendix-ranked analyses may be added without changing this strategy.\\\",\n+    \\\"planned_subsections\\\": [\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Complete Case, Budget and Seed Results\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Tables of candidate_curves, all baseline_curves, counts, paired_intervals and graph descriptors for every final case/seed. Preserve intervals that include zero and the repeated nature of algorithmic seeds. Include recorded original/edited rank intervals where useful, without inventing per-budget intervals absent from the evidence.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Influence Arithmetic and Finite-Change Diagnostics\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Explain unit-outcome derivatives versus binary-flip signed shifts, the frozen original Hessian and independent exact refits, using the selected program and public contract as method documentation. Tabulate recorded influence_errors by case/budget and method_audit and control outcomes. The overall finite-change discrepancy is 0.14315313656317594; do not interpret it as a rate of invalid results or prove hidden implementation internals from a passing audit.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.metric.influence_error\\\", \\\"final.metric.control_error\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Nested Flip-Path Construction and Reproducibility\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Document the centered sum-loss ridge-1 objective, sufficient-statistic representation, width-two generator, selected-position swaps, unused-row replacements, affected-prefix caching, strict complete-path acceptance and incumbent fallback from the available selected source. Report source-declared bounds as settings, not measured usage: 128 optional proposals, 72 additional converged fits at dimension at most 64 and 24 otherwise, and a two-second soft optional-search deadline. An ongoing fit is not interrupted; load-dependent truncation limits bitwise reproducibility. Include the recorded final seeds, observable durations, program-tree digest and exact existing dependency/data-acquisition files. Do not invent per-method runtimes or claim reproduction has been rerun. Final evidence anchors the evaluated bundle; implementation details are corroborated by the named program and public contract, not inferred from metric values.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\", \\\"final.qualification.status\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Data Provenance and Scope of Comparability\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Use task/resources/final/manifest.json and task/prepare_data.py as existing provenance documentation alongside the final graph/count evidence: Arena normalized document-connected groups, unique NBA games, reciprocal-row handling, content-disjoint partition policy, source snapshots/checksums and license records where actually available. Distinguish a manifest assertion from an independently rerun verification. Explain fractional ties, NBA home effects, season-specific fitting and unequal graph coverage. No MT-Bench, expert/judge or block-deletion results can be added.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"Evaluation Outcome and Claim Boundaries\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Record the completed and qualified final evaluation using final.qualification.*, separately from point estimates and publication judgment. Explain that numerical audits and four controls have limited scope, that candidate diagnostics are marked unverified, and that no comparative-superiority gate is implied. Do not invent absent gate diagnostics. If later authoritative evidence reports failed qualification, update the main claims, review, audit and revisions together; do not silently retain a qualified characterization.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"final.qualification.status\\\", \\\"final.qualification.outcome\\\", \\\"final.qualification.correct\\\", \\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      },\n+      {\n+        \\\"heading\\\": \\\"LLM Usage\\\",\n+        \\\"grounded_content\\\": \\\"Disclose the documented assistance with ideation, candidate-source preparation, reference-query planning and paper framing/writing. Separate static preparation statements from actual recorded evaluator execution. Use source paths and assistant logs as provenance, without claiming any undocumented model-generated judgments of the empirical data, prohibited-source access, or literature reading. Redact identifying paths and keep the submission anonymous.\\\",\n+        \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"result.top_program_01\\\", \\\"final.evidence.episodes\\\"]\n+      }\n+    ]\n+  },\n+  \\\"forbidden_headings\\\": [\n+    \\\"Search Progression\\\",\n+    \\\"Campaign Timeline\\\",\n+    \\\"Milestones\\\",\n+    \\\"First Valid Result\\\",\n+    \\\"Experiment A / Experiment B\\\",\n+    \\\"Phase 1 / Phase 2\\\",\n+    \\\"Round-by-Round Improvements\\\",\n+    \\\"From Failure to Winner\\\",\n+    \\\"Architecture Ablations\\\",\n+    \\\"Matched MT-Bench Deletion Results\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"forbidden_phrases\\\": [\n+    \\\"first valid result\\\",\n+    \\\"we then tried\\\",\n+    \\\"subsequent improvements\\\",\n+    \\\"next-best\\\",\n+    \\\"later variants\\\",\n+    \\\"winning iteration\\\",\n+    \\\"correctness rate\\\",\n+    \\\"correct and eligible\\\",\n+    \\\"eligible\\\",\n+    \\\"worker_01\\\",\n+    \\\"worker_02\\\",\n+    \\\"combined_score\\\",\n+    \\\"rubric\\\",\n+    \\\"state-of-the-art leaderboard attack\\\",\n+    \\\"certified minimum manipulation budget\\\",\n+    \\\"exactly exposure-matched\\\",\n+    \\\"all NBA comparisons are significant\\\",\n+    \\\"sports evaluation is causally more robust\\\",\n+    \\\"the exchange component explains the gain\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"notes_for_writer\\\": [\n+    \\\"Organize thesis-first: Introduction; Related Work; Ranking Sensitivity and Perturbation Model; Influence-Guided Exact-Refit Stress Testing; Evaluation Design; Results and Conditional Uncertainty; Discussion and Limitations; Conclusion. Arena and NBA are evidence blocks for one question, not two chronologically ordered experiments.\\\",\n+    \\\"Plan approximately 8.5 body pages including figures and captions: abstract/introduction 1.2, related work 0.6, estimand/model 1.0, method 1.4, evaluation design 1.1, results 2.1, discussion/limitations 0.9, conclusion 0.2. These are layout targets, not measured results. The venue permits 8–9 pages excluding references, with an 8-page body valid only if its final page is at least 75% full. Spend space on equations, clear comparison design, graph/count context, complete uncertainty and limitations, not a search log, speculative theory or decorative material. Rebalance within the cap rather than padding.\\\",\n+    \\\"Inspected .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/iclr/paper.tex and paper.sty: article is single-column, textwidth 5.5 inches and textheight 9 inches on letter paper. There is no separate half-page conference column; column width equals full text width. All three required figures therefore use ordinary full-text-width figures. Keep practical final-size font targets rather than shrinking dense assets.\\\",\n+    \\\"The supplied scaffold enables final-copy mode and contains an author string: remove that mode and author identity for the anonymous ICLR 2026 submission, omit affiliations, acknowledgements and funding, and retain any orchestrator-owned watermark block unchanged. Do not claim official latest-template provenance has been independently verified merely because the supplied style is available; document that provenance at the writing/compilation stage. The task contract mentions a different venue, but the current explicit ICLR 2026 venue brief governs this strategy.\\\",\n+    \\\"State the model explicitly: sum of logistic losses plus one-half the squared parameter norm, participant scores centered, optional NBA home covariate regularized with the same fixed coefficient. Ties contribute fractional outcomes but are uneditable. Nominal costs use all usable rows; report exact floor-rounded costs alongside the nominal fractions. Distinguish method internal displacement-first lexicographic selection from the reader-facing inversion-fraction endpoint; they are not identical objectives.\\\",\n+    \\\"Use final.metric.* and final.evidence.episodes for final quantitative claims, and final.qualification.* only for qualification facts. The actual outcome here is qualified, not not_qualified. Absence of downstream_study does not invalidate the independent completed final evaluation. Preserve this separation in later drafting, review, audit and revision. Unknown gate causes remain unknown; neither positive metrics nor publication eligibility override an adverse outcome in other runs.\\\",\n+    \\\"Private-only provenance context: selection corroboration comes from result.top_program_01 and the best-program manifest, while the final program-tree digest is recorded independently. No study.* namespace is supplied; omit unsupported selection differences and attempt-count claims rather than synthesizing aliases. Do not compare the earlier candidate as a final baseline or label differing search submissions as controlled ablations.\\\",\n+    \\\"The main paper must say that these are feasible observed-outcome counterfactual changes, not evidence of historical vote rigging, population preference change or attacker access in deployed systems. Finding a disruptive path gives an attainable sensitivity witness, not an optimal attack, a lower bound on necessary changes, or a certificate of robustness.\\\",\n+    \\\"Uncertainty is conditional on fixed selected interventions and fixed panels. Thirty resamples give coarse percentile endpoints; three seeds are not three independent datasets; no multiple-comparison correction or adaptive-reselection uncertainty is established. Keep the inconclusive NBA evidence in the main text and figure, not only in the supplement.\\\",\n+    \\\"Do not invent component ablations, alternative ridge sweeps, deletion studies, matched human/judge data, successful target reversals, runtime speedups, unseen-model or temporal generalization, or architectures. A mechanistic description of exchange is supported by code, but attributing the observed advantage specifically to exchange is not supported by a controlled final ablation.\\\",\n+    \\\"Quantitative plots must be regenerated from recorded arrays by saved scripts and exported as vector PDF plus PNG at 300 DPI; LaTeX must reference the PDF whenever it exists. Use the same four method colors throughout, colorblind-safe markers, abbreviated case labels and shared legends. Derived seed means must be explicitly labeled summaries of the recorded values, never new experimental observations.\\\",\n+    \\\"Plan exactly one generate-concept-figure overview. The orchestrator owns rendering; the writer only wires the figure and its manifest/prompt-log entries according to the skill. If an editable vector export yields a PDF, use that PDF in LaTeX; otherwise require the full-width PNG to be regenerated at at least 2400 pixels wide. Column-only raster assets elsewhere require at least 1200 pixels. Never upscale a raster, fabricate diagram measurements, or invoke the image workflow during this strategy stage.\\\",\n+    \\\"After references, use clearpage, bibliography, clearpage, appendix, and a substantive Supplementary Information section. Include the separate LLM Usage section there. Keep essential baselines, uncertainty and limitations in the main body. Later authoritative appendix-ranked analyses belong in Supplementary Information without retroactively changing this strategy.\\\",\n+    \\\"Safe related work remains a writing prerequisite: the current bibliography is not a verified reading list. Most retrieval results are irrelevant and metadata records alone do not establish that an original was read. Only use admissible relevant originals actually read and citation keys synchronized with the supplied BibTeX/provenance; if needed, repair bibliography grounding in the appropriate later stage. Do not fill space with unrelated retrieved works or claim comprehensive novelty. Do not infer the prohibited work's identity, use citation expansion, or access uncertain related pages; stop and log any accidental encounter without continuing.\\\",\n+    \\\"Only strategy outputs are created in this stage: no paper.tex, claims_grounding.json, new scientific experiments or final-paper validation. Validate JSON shape, source-ID resolution, figure budgets and memo agreement only. No required empirical result is deferred to a hypothetical future experiment.\\\"\n+  ],\n+  \\\"failure_reason\\\": \\\"\\\"\n+}\n*** Add File: paper_strategy.md\n+# Paper Framing Strategy\n+\n+**Status:** ready for a grounded standalone-paper plan, not a claim of publication readiness.  \n+**Family:** \"'`paper_standalone`, using `write-paper-standalone`.  \n+**Provisional title:** *Exact-Refit Stress Tests for Bradley–Terry Rankings*.  \n+**Venue:** anonymous ICLR 2026 submission; 8–9 body pages excluding references.\n+\n+## Central Question and Thesis\n+\n+**Question.** How much can small, matched-budget binary-outcome changes disrupt fitted Bradley–Terry orderings on the observed Arena and NBA panels, and how consistently do exact-refitted guided interventions exceed simple controls?\n+\n+**Thesis.** On these fixed panels, influence-guided flip-path exchange produces larger budget-averaged pairwise-order disruption point estimates than three matched-budget baselines. Conditional bootstrap evidence supports a clearer advantage on Arena than across NBA seasons. This is an empirical sensitivity study, not a proof of an optimal attack, population generalization or a causal difference between evaluation designs.\n+\n+This story uses one shared estimator/intervention with condition-specific evidence blocks: a crowdsourced Arena panel and season-specific sports panels. They are neither matched datasets nor a controlled experiment on evaluation design. NBA'\"'s home-effect adaptation belongs in the model description, not a separate method family.\n+\n+## Evidence and Qualification Audit\n+\n+Read \"'`paper_data.json.final_evaluation` independently of other study metadata. Its reported status is completed, outcome qualified and correctness flag true, grounded respectively in `final.qualification.status`, `final.qualification.outcome` and `final.qualification.correct`. Do not turn these reported outcomes into publication approval, universal validity or comparative superiority. Candidate diagnostic trust is explicitly unverified; use recorded independent refit/audit evidence only within its documented scope.\n+\n+There is no `downstream_study` or `study.*` source namespace. Do not fabricate a campaign classification, attempt accounting or search-score differences under that namespace. The available selected source and `results/best_program_manifest.json` corroborate the identity in `result.top_program_01`; the final record separately supplies a program-tree digest. No independent recomputation of that tree digest is claimed. Keep development provenance separate from final results, and omit an original-candidate performance comparison because no matched final evaluation of that comparator is supplied.\n+\n+The completed final evaluation is usable even without downstream-study metadata. In another run, a completed but unqualified outcome would require explicit failed-qualification disclosure throughout drafting, review, audit and revision; neither retained metrics nor publication eligibility could erase it. Here the actual reported outcome is qualified. Never invent absent gate diagnostics or attribute an unknown failure to performance, validity or adaptivity.\n+\n+### Decisive Grounded Results\n+\n+- `final.evidence.episodes` contains three final seeds, 401, 503 and 607, each with Arena and NBA 2011–2015. These are algorithmic seeds, not independent datasets.\n+- Primary endpoint: participant-pair ordering reversals divided by the number of participant pairs, with the fixed participant-index tie rule. Reconstructing it from stored original and edited scores exactly reproduces every stored candidate endpoint. Larger values mean stronger disruption, not improved ranking accuracy.\n+- Nominal fractions are 0.1%, 0.5% and 1% of all usable rows, floored to integers. Ties remain in fitting and in the denominator but cannot be flipped. Arena costs are 43, 216 and 432 flips; NBA 2012 costs are 1, 5 and 10; other final NBA seasons use 1, 6 and 13. Report counts alongside nominal fractions.\n+- Final overall disruption values are 0.055641534391534395 for the proposed bundle, 0.00935242200328407 for uniform random, 0.011150133225384662 for degree-quartile matched, and 0.007573891625615763 for close-margin flips. Source each from the corresponding `final.metric.*` entry, not from search results.\n+- Explain the weighting: equal budgets and seeds within case, equal NBA seasons within the sports family, and equal weight for the two design families. Do not pool rows or overweight NBA because it has five panels.\n+- Arena'\"'s paired intervals have positive lower endpoints against all three baselines in all recorded seeds. Multiple NBA intervals include zero; NBA 2013–2015 do so for all three baselines across all seeds. This uncertainty is essential main-body evidence, not supplemental fine print.\n+- These intervals concern budget-averaged disruption under fixed intervention plans, not each individual budget point. They use 30 grouped bootstrap replicates per final case/seed. No reselection, seed pooling, design-family confidence interval, multiplicity adjustment or independent-population replication is established.\n+- Final graphs have 64 Arena participants and 30 in each NBA season. Graph coverage, finite-change influence discrepancies and fixed regularization constrain interpretation. Do not fit causal explanations to those descriptors.\n+\n+## Explicit Framing Decision\n+\n+There is no edit-mode context or prior manuscript: \"'`previous_paper/`, `aggregated/` and `extra_tasks/` are absent. The JSON status `prior_paper_story_status: rejected` rejects the earlier prospective story, not an unseen manuscript.\n+\n+| Candidate framing | Decision and grounded reason |\n+| --- | --- |\n+| Preserve exposure-matched MT-Bench block deletion with local updates | Reject: evaluated outcomes are binary flips on Arena/NBA, not question-block deletions or matched human/judge contrasts. |\n+| Broaden to a general deletion/flip robustness family | Reject as the thesis: the shared family would contain unmeasured interventions and unavailable matching. |\n+| Recenter on attainable finite-flip sensitivity with exact refits | Select: directly supported by final case/budget/baseline evidence and uncertainty, with two real evaluation designs. |\n+| Tell a search-winner or component-improvement story | Reject: search order is not the scientific question, and no controlled component-ablation bundle exists. |\n+\n+Direct inspection of the selected `program.py` and `IMPLEMENTATION.md` supports sufficient-statistic aggregation, a width-two exact-refitted path generator, complete-path swaps/replacements and fallback. Do not import the different width-four branch as the selected mechanism. The intervention interface supplies no provenance-aware deletion or cross-design matching. No old title or figure plan is retained by inertia.\n+\n+## Narrow Method Set\n+\n+1. **Proposed:** influence-guided exact-refit flip-path exchange, treated as one evaluated bundle. Explain its original-Hessian screening, nested paths, exact-refitted comparisons, affected-prefix caching and complete incumbent fallback. Do not attribute the aggregate advantage specifically to exchange without an ablation.\n+2. **Baseline:** uniform random binary-outcome flips, using the recorded stream averages.\n+3. **Baseline:** degree-sum-quartile-matched random flips, conditional on the actual selected prefixes. This is approximate exposure control, not exact endpoint/content matching.\n+4. **Baseline:** smallest absolute fitted matchup-margin flips.\n+5. **Supporting diagnostics only:** independent refits and no-op, rotated-priority, reset and explicitly synthetic constant-zero checks. These are not additional competitive algorithms or architectural ablations.\n+\n+Define the fixed model: summed logistic losses plus one-half the squared parameter norm, centered participant scores and an optional regularized NBA home coefficient. Preserve ridge 1 and the fixed tie rule. Distinguish the method'\"'s displacement-first lexicographic internal objective from the inversion-fraction endpoint. A mathematically correct local derivative does not imply accurate finite-change ranking predictions; exact refits determine measured endpoints.\n+\n+## Required Figures and Readability Budgets\n+\n+The inspected ICLR template uses \"'`article`; `paper.sty` sets a **single 5.5-inch text column and 9-inch text height**. Thus ordinary column width equals full text width. There is no two-column `figure*` geometry to borrow, and half-width figures would unnecessarily constrain labels. All required figures use the full 5.5-inch text width. Heights below exclude captions.\n+\n+### 1. `sensitivity_overview`: Early Conceptual Overview\n+\n+- **Generator:** `generate-concept-figure`, exactly once in the plan; rendering belongs to the orchestrator, not this strategy stage.\n+- **Placement:** page 1 or 2; full text width; approximately 1.6–1.9 inches high; final labels at least 9 pt.\n+- **Content:** two sparse side-by-side panels. The first defines fixed observed comparisons, uneditable ties and legal nested flips. The second relates influence screening, complete-path selection/exchange, independent exact refits, three matched-budget baselines and fixed-plan grouped uncertainty. Arena and NBA are unequal evidence blocks, not causally linked designs.\n+- **Budget:** at most two panels, two per row, six conceptual categories and four semantic series per panel. No invented empirical graph or rank-change example, decorative architecture or measured values.\n+- **Grounding:** `final.evidence.episodes`, with mechanism labels corroborated by the selected implementation and public task contract.\n+\n+### 2. `final_disruption_comparison`: All Cases and Budgets\n+\n+- **Generator:** matplotlib; grouped dots, not connected trajectories.\n+- **Placement:** full text width; three vertically stacked panels; approximately 3.7–4.2 inches high, 8–9 pt labels.\n+- **Content:** one panel per nominal fraction; six case categories; four method series. Use a common metric scale and one shared legend. Mark descriptive means of the three recorded seeds; put individual values in the supplement and actual integer costs in a main-text table.\n+- **Budget:** at most three panels, one per row, six categories and four series per panel. No invented error bars or interpretation of seeds as datasets; the next figure supplies paired uncertainty.\n+- **Grounding:** stored `candidate_curves`, `baseline_curves` and `counts` under `final.evidence.episodes`. Seed means are transparent arithmetic summaries of recorded values, not new observations.\n+\n+### 3. `paired_effect_uncertainty`: Conditional Effects and Null-Compatible Cases\n+\n+- **Generator:** matplotlib; forest plot with a clear zero reference.\n+- **Placement:** full text width; three vertical baseline panels; approximately 4.6–5.2 inches high, 8–9 pt labels. Do not squeeze three forest panels horizontally or shrink this to half width.\n+- **Content:** six cases per panel; three modestly offset seed-specific intervals per case. Use recorded budget-averaged `paired_intervals` exactly. Keep Arena'\"'s clearer advantage beside NBA's inconclusive comparisons.\n+- **Budget:** at most three panels, one per row, six categories and three seed series per panel.\n+- **Statistical labeling:** show interval segments without fabricated centers. If a point marker is necessary, compute and label the mean of the corresponding recorded bootstrap paired effects, rather than silently inserting the original-sample effect or interval midpoint. Do not pool seeds or claim simultaneous coverage.\n+- **Grounding:** \"'`final.evidence.episodes`. Budget-specific point comparisons and budget-averaged intervals are distinct estimands and must be labeled accordingly.\n+\n+### Export Contract\n+\n+Save plotting scripts and input mappings. Export quantitative figures as vector PDF and PNG at 300 DPI; include the PDF in LaTeX whenever available. Keep method colors and markers consistent and colorblind-safe. For the concept figure, preserve editable source and use a vector PDF if available; otherwise regenerate the full-width raster at at least 2400 pixels wide. Other column-only rasters require at least 1200 pixels. Never upscale an existing raster. The writer wires concept-figure manifest/prompt-log entries according to the skill; it does not run the orchestrator-owned pipeline.\n+\n+## Body Layout and Page Use\n+\n+Target approximately **8.5 body pages**, including captions and figures, within the explicit 8–9-page venue budget. An exactly eight-page body must leave its last page at least 75% full. Use scientific depth, not padding:\n+\n+| Scientific section | Approximate page allocation | Value supplied |\n+| --- | ---: | --- |\n+| Abstract and introduction | 1.2 | Problem, scoped contributions and early overview |\n+| Related work | 0.6 | Relevant actually read methods and positioning, not retrieval filler |\n+| Ranking sensitivity and perturbation model | 1.0 | Estimand, fixed objective, ties, costs and order conventions |\n+| Influence-guided exact-refit stress testing | 1.4 | Bundle, derivative/refit distinction, nested path construction and limits |\n+| Evaluation design | 1.1 | Panel provenance, graph/count table, baselines, weighting and bootstrap |\n+| Results and conditional uncertainty | 2.1 | All-case comparison, final aggregate table, paired intervals and inconclusive cases |\n+| Discussion and limitations | 0.9 | Scope, approximation, adaptive selection, unequal graphs and no causal claims |\n+| Conclusion | 0.2 | Narrow answer to the research question |\n+\n+These are layout targets rather than empirical values. Rebalance within the cap; do not invent theory, sweeps, baselines or chronology to reach it. The substantive model/protocol explanation and uncertainty analysis justify the space even without component ablations.\n+\n+The supplied template scaffold includes final-copy mode and an author identity. The writer must remove both for anonymous review, omit affiliations/acknowledgements/funding, avoid identifying links and preserve the orchestrator-owned watermark block unchanged. The current ICLR brief governs venue choice despite older task-contract venue language. Inspect and document official template provenance later rather than claiming the supplied style proves latest-edition compliance now.\n+\n+## Supplementary Information After References\n+\n+Purpose: provide complete existing evidence and reproducibility depth without hiding evidence essential to the thesis. Use `clearpage`, bibliography, `clearpage`, appendix and a substantive `Supplementary Information` section in the final paper. Route later authoritative appendix-ranked analyses here without retroactively revising this strategy.\n+\n+1. **Complete Case, Budget and Seed Results.** All candidate/baseline endpoints, integer counts, intervals and graph descriptors, including null-compatible cases. Use recorded rank intervals where useful without manufacturing absent budget-specific uncertainty. Source: `final.evidence.episodes`.\n+2. **Influence Arithmetic and Finite-Change Diagnostics.** Distinguish unit derivatives, signed flip shifts and nonlinear discrepancies; tabulate recorded errors, method audits and control outcomes. The recorded overall discrepancy is 0.14315313656317594, not an invalidity rate. Sources: `final.evidence.episodes`, `final.metric.influence_error`, `final.metric.control_error`; corroborate method equations with code and the public contract.\n+3. **Nested Flip-Path Construction and Reproducibility.** Document the available selected code'\"'s width-two generator, swaps/replacements, cache and fallback. Source-declared optional limits are 128 proposals, 72 added converged fits at dimension at most 64 and 24 otherwise, plus a two-second soft deadline; these are not measured usage or a hard interruption bound. Include recorded seeds/durations/digest and existing dependency/acquisition files, never invented per-method runtimes or claims of a fresh reproduction. Sources: \"'`final.evidence.episodes`, `final.qualification.status`, corroborated by the explicitly named implementation.\n+4. **Data Provenance and Scope of Comparability.** Explain normalized Arena document groups, unique NBA games, reciprocal-row handling, partition policy, ties, home effects, season-specific fitting and unequal coverage. Use `task/resources/final/manifest.json` and `task/prepare_data.py` as available documentation, distinguishing manifest assertions from independently rerun checks. Anchor empirical graph/count evidence to `final.evidence.episodes`; do not invent missing licenses/checksums or add MT-Bench results.\n+5. **Evaluation Outcome and Claim Boundaries.** Separate reported completed/qualified status, numerical audits, unverified candidate diagnostics and publication judgment. Preserve all limitations and unknown diagnostics in review/audit/revision. Sources: `final.qualification.status`, `final.qualification.outcome`, `final.qualification.correct`, `final.evidence.episodes`.\n+6. **LLM Usage.** A separate disclosure section describing documented ideation, code preparation, reference planning, framing and writing assistance. Distinguish static preparation from recorded evaluator execution; omit unsupported literature-reading or empirical-judging claims. Use available assistant logs, `result.top_program_01` and `final.evidence.episodes` for traceability; redact identifying paths.\n+\n+Source IDs above are existing registered anchors; file paths supply additional documentary support rather than pretending that metric entries independently prove source-code internals or provenance checks.\n+\n+## Claims, References and Wording Guardrails\n+\n+Do not infer historical misconduct, attacker access, global optimality, a minimum required corruption budget, population preference change, unseen-model performance or temporal generalization. An attainable disruption is a sensitivity witness, not a robustness certificate. Approximate exposure control does not make the two data designs comparable in a causal sense. No final component ablations, ridge sweeps, deletions or matched human/judge analyses exist.\n+\n+The existing bibliography is a retrieval output, not an already verified reading list: provenance is metadata-only and many entries are irrelevant. Related work must use admissible relevant originals actually read, with synchronized BibTeX/provenance keys. Do not cite irrelevant records to fill space, claim comprehensive novelty, perform citation expansion, infer the prohibited study'\"'s identity or access uncertain related pages. If forbidden material is encountered accidentally, stop and record location and amount read. No such encounter is claimed in this framing stage.\n+\n+**Forbidden headings:** Search Progression; Campaign Timeline; Milestones; First Valid Result; Experiment A / Experiment B; Phase 1 / Phase 2; Round-by-Round Improvements; From Failure to Winner; Architecture Ablations; Matched MT-Bench Deletion Results.\n+\n+**Forbidden visible phrases:** first valid result; we then tried; subsequent improvements; next-best; later variants; winning iteration; correctness rate; correct and eligible; eligible; worker_01; worker_02; combined_score; rubric; state-of-the-art leaderboard attack; certified minimum manipulation budget; exactly exposure-matched; all NBA comparisons are significant; sports evaluation is causally more robust; the exchange component explains the gain. Internal identifiers in this strategy are private provenance only, not recommendations for reader-facing labels.\n+\n+## Handoff and Stage Limits\n+\n+Implement the required figures first, preserve their readability budgets, and keep both the strong and inconclusive evidence visible. Quantitative final claims use \"'`final.metric.*` or `final.evidence.episodes`; qualification facts use `final.qualification.*`. Search provenance is not final replication and unscored work is not a measured loss.\n+\n+This stage produces only the strategy memo and JSON plus append-only memory updates. It does not draft `paper.tex`, create `claims_grounding.json`, run candidate/evaluator experiments, generate figures or perform final-paper validation. Check strategy JSON structure, source-ID resolution, figure budgets and memo consistency only. No necessary empirical result is deferred to a hypothetical later experiment.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH'","aggregated_output":"Added paper_strategy.json\nAdded paper_strategy.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
